Abiquo''s core business revolves around its cloud orchestration software, which enables clients to manage private, public, and hybrid cloud infrastructures from a single, unified portal. The platform is designed to be hardware and hypervisor independent, supporting a wide range of technologies including VMware, Hyper-V, KVM, Docker containers, and major public clouds like AWS, Microsoft Azure, and Google Cloud Platform. This allows organizations to avoid vendor lock-in and manage diverse IT environments with greater efficiency and control. The company primarily targets service providers, resellers, and large enterprises that need to manage complex, multi-tenant cloud environments securely. 

The business model centers on licensing its software, which clients can white-label and offer under their own brand. Abiquo provides flexible pricing structures, including consumption-based and fixed-price models, enabling its customers to create and price cloud service bundles for their end-users. Key features of the Abiquo platform include automation for service provisioning and scaling, comprehensive cost management with real-time analytics, and robust security through role-based access control (RBAC) and multi-level policies. The platform gives IT teams real-time visibility into resource utilization, helping them optimize spending and make data-driven decisions. By unifying management, Abiquo helps organizations reduce operational complexity, improve service delivery, and accelerate their go-to-market strategies for new cloud offerings. 

