 The company operates on a software-as-a-service (SaaS) business model, charging clients a monthly subscription fee based on the number of rooms and services utilized. Its primary objective is to empower independent hoteliers, who often rely on a patchwork of complex legacy systems, to streamline operations and increase direct bookings, thereby reducing their dependency on costly online travel agencies (OTAs). The market opportunity is significant, with over 80% of Europe''s 700,000 hospitality properties being independent establishments with fewer than 50 rooms. 

 Often described as a ''Shopify for hotels'', Amenitiz offers an integrated suite of tools. This includes a user-friendly website builder with an integrated booking engine, a channel manager to synchronize availability and rates across over 120 OTAs, and a core Property Management System (PMS) for daily operations like guest management, invoicing, and communication. The platform also features AmenitizPay, a module for automating and securing online and on-site payments. Significant milestones include raising a €6.5 million seed round in late 2021, followed by a landmark $30 million Series A round in April 2022, the largest ever for a SaaS company in Spain at the time. In October 2022, Amenitiz acquired Ododo, a training platform for hoteliers, to further enhance its value proposition. 

