The firm operates on a B2C model, allowing migrants anywhere in the world to purchase health plans for their relatives through a fully digital platform. This model generates revenue through the sale of these health plans. The target market is migrants who are supporting loved ones in their countries of origin, with a significant focus on Latin America and Southeast Asia, including countries like Venezuela, the Dominican Republic, Mexico, and the Philippines. Asistensi’s business strategy involves forming partnerships with local healthcare providers in the countries where the beneficiaries reside, such as the collaboration with Maxicare in the Philippines.

Asistensi offers accessible health plans that cover day-to-day ailments, common illnesses, and medical emergencies. The plans are designed to be comprehensive and easy to access, featuring 100% digital onboarding without the need for medical admission exams. Key services include 24/7 unlimited telemedicine, ambulance services, primary care at home or in a clinic, home and in-clinic laboratory tests, medication delivery, and access to major hospitals for hospitalization and surgery. A notable feature is the coverage for pre-existing conditions and eligibility for beneficiaries up to 85 years old, which addresses a significant gap in the traditional insurance market. The company emphasizes continuous patient follow-up from its medical team as a key differentiator.

Keywords: insurtech, migrant healthcare, digital health plans, cross-border insurance, telemedicine services, remittance for health, family healthcare plans, Latin America healthcare, Southeast Asia healthcare, affordable insurance, digital onboarding, emergency medical coverage, primary care services, healthcare for diaspora, remote healthcare support, health insurance for relatives, Venezuelan migrants, Filipino migrant workers, expatriate services, global healthcare access', '["Health Platform","Insurtech Distribution and Brokerage","Reduced Inequalities (#10)","Venture Capital","LandH Insurance","SaaS","page builders","Good Health And Well-Being (#3)","frameworks and libraries","communication and collaboration","Fintech","other advertising software","domain name services","it infrastructure","web frameworks","tag management","Insurance","widgets","web servers","Hard Tech","Migrants","programming languages","Commission","Breakout stage","advertising","payment processing","web and application servers","miscellaneous","programming","cloud infrastructure computing","office suites","Health Insurance","intelligence and analytics","analytics","Sustainable Development Goals","operating systems & computing languages","cloud hosting","web analytics","platform as a service","Health","b2c","javascript frameworks","Marketplace & ecommerce","social networks","continuous integration","web hosting"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 63.86, 240, 0, 0, 43249983, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:55:09.655Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:55:09.655Z');

The platform is designed for modern go-to-market (GTM) teams and allows users to build, automate, and customize their CRM to fit their specific business models and workflows. Attio''s core features include a flexible data model with custom objects and attributes, real-time data synchronization and collaboration, automated data enrichment, and an intelligent automation engine. The system automatically creates and enriches contact and company profiles by syncing with users'' email and calendars, capturing data points like job titles, employee counts, and interaction history. It also offers advanced reporting and analytics, pipeline and deal management, and an App SDK that allows users to build custom applications directly within the platform. 

Attio operates on a freemium business model, offering several pricing tiers, including a Free plan for small teams, as well as Plus, Pro, and Enterprise plans for scaling businesses with more advanced needs. The company targets high-growth technology companies and serves over 5,000 paying customers, including notable names like Lovable, Modal, Replicate, and Public. Attio has successfully raised a total of $141 million over seven funding rounds. Its latest funding was a Series B round, which included investors like GV (Google Ventures), Redpoint Ventures, Balderton Capital, and Point Nine. 

Keywords: customer relationship management, AI-native CRM, go-to-market teams, data-driven CRM, flexible data model, workflow automation, real-time data sync, automated data enrichment, custom CRM, sales pipeline management, contact management, business process automation, SaaS, go-to-market software, relationship intelligence, collaborative CRM, CRM for startups, GTM automation, sales intelligence, lead management', '["corporate","data management","database","data security","human resource management system","Venture Capital","recruitment marketing","deal execution","editors","ad exchanges","Core AI","Productivity Tools","Subscription","SaaS","sales enablement","marketing automation","customer relationship management","human resources","page builders","Angel","communication and collaboration","development","content management system","performance","marketing analytics","software development","Reporting Software","payroll management and benefits administration","it infrastructure","web frameworks","customer data platforms","b2b","web platform extensions","Business Analytics","Artificial Intelligence","team collaboration","widgets","software framework","api management","programming languages","advertising","CRM","pre-employment assessment","site search","web & portal technology","miscellaneous","programming","AI Applications","cloud infrastructure computing","business intelligence","governance-risk and compliance","account-based marketing","javascript libraries","wordpress plugins","Data Analytics","intelligence and analytics","Late stage","Enterprise Software","analytics","devops","issue trackers","web analytics","Marketing","platform as a service","uk is8 digital and technologies","application development & management","font scripts","CRM & Sales","blogs","applicant tracking systems","design","ui frameworks","certificates","continuous integration","containerization","data management platforms","web tools and plugins","web hosting"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded