 The company operates in the InsurTech and Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) markets, providing a digital-first, cloud-based platform designed to manage the entire collision and claims process. Its core offering, the Connected Collision Management Platform, provides end-to-end solutions starting from the moment a collision occurs. This platform facilitates automated collision capture through various interfaces (aCall/bCall/eCall), enables self-service online reporting for customers, and aggregates collision data from multiple sources. For its business clients, Axitech’s technology creates a more seamless, harmonized, and less stressful post-accident experience for the end-user, which in turn helps brands improve customer loyalty and unlock new revenue streams. By integrating the fragmented supply chain of roadside assistance, repair management, and claims processing, the platform offers a unified and proactive service. 

 Financially, Axitech is a venture capital-backed entity, having secured funding from several institutional investors and angel investors, including a Series A round led by Balderton Capital. The company has undergone multiple funding rounds to support its growth, including an angel round in 2009 and several later-stage VC rounds, with the most recent being in January 2024. The business model is centered on providing its software to automotive and insurance partners, enabling them to offer enhanced, branded collision support and embedded claims journeys within their own services. This approach allows clients to better manage insurance claims, increase engagement through personalized experiences, and ultimately derive greater value from their connected car data. 

 Keywords: collision management, claims management, connected vehicle ecosystem, InsurTech, SaaS, automotive technology, FNOL, e-FNOL, claims orchestration, connected car data, digital claims processing, accident management, post-collision services, automotive OEMs, insurance carriers, brand loyalty, customer experience, venture capital-backed, Matt Hodges, Balderton Capital', '["database","Venture Capital","editors","Subscription","SaaS","Angel","frameworks and libraries","content management system","Maintenance","performance","system analytics & monitoring","software development","wikis","b2b","web platform extensions","tag management","widgets","web servers","search engines","api management","content delivery network","programming languages","audio-video-graphics","programming","Connected Car","cloud infrastructure computing","governance-risk and compliance","e-commerce","javascript libraries","wordpress plugins","intelligence and analytics","video players","analytics","devops","Transportation","wordpress themes","web analytics","platform as a service","a-b testing","application development & management","consent management","Early stage","blogs","continuous integration","cookie compliance","machine learning","Autonomous & Sensor Tech","captcha","web tools and plugins","web hosting"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 46.55, 460, 0, 0, 23045445, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"year":2021,"revenue":1022727,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":19},{"year":2022,"revenue":1136363,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":20},{"year":2023,"revenue":1136363,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":23045445,"employees":20},{"year":2024,"revenue":1136363,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":23045445,"employees":13},{"year":2025,"revenue":1136363,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":23045445,"employees":17},{"year":2026,"revenue":1136363,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"va