The company''s core product is a multi-omics platform that uses a single blood sample for AI-driven transcriptomic analysis. This platform integrates genomics and transcriptomics to analyze over 15,000 genes and 330 metabolic pathways, translating molecular signals into insights about the functional health and biological age of more than 47 tissues. The technology is designed to detect organ-level deterioration and molecular signs of tissue dysfunction before clinical symptoms appear, enabling a shift from reactive to predictive healthcare. 

Initially concentrating on women''s health, BASE4''s AI models are trained exclusively on female biological data to address the historical underrepresentation of women in clinical trials and medical research. The company is launching three initial clinical programs: fertility and women''s health (focusing on ovarian biology and menopause), preventive health for early detection, and applications for pharmaceutical research, including pharmacotranscriptomics to identify early signs of tissue-level toxicity. The business model appears to be B2B and SaaS-based, targeting clinics and certified health professionals. The first commercial product, a women-centered blood test, is scheduled to be offered in Barcelona starting January 2026 via a beta program, with a broader European and US rollout to follow. 

In April 2026, BASE4 Biosciences announced it had raised a $1 million pre-seed funding round supported by investors including Kfund, Itnig, Masia VC, and Baobab Ventures. This capital is intended to advance the development of its platform and support the initial product launch. The company has also received over €7 million in total research grant funding to date. 

Keywords: precision health, preventive medicine, transcriptomics, multi-omics, AI in healthcare, biological age, early disease detection, organ health, women''s health, fertility, menopause, molecular diagnostics, blood-based testing, genomics, Sant Pau Research Institute, Pol Cervera, Jose Manuel Soria, pharmacotranscriptomics, liquid biopsy, personalized medicine, digital health, biotech', '["medical testing","Venture Capital","BioTechnology","b2b","Artificial Intelligence","Commission","Biomarkers","Genetics and genomics","Gender Equality (#5)","Sustainable Development Goals","Health","Early stage"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 69.47, 2000, 0, 0, 4545453, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:56:04.243Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:56:04.243Z');

Bcome.biz''s platform allows businesses to take data-driven decisions, helping them drive growth and reach their goals with certainty. It also enables businesses to share their sustainability insights with their audience in a simple and engaging way, which can build trust, boost sales, and show their commitment to sustainability. 

The platform also offers features that allow businesses to benchmark their products against industry standards, map their suppliers, and automate sustainability tasks. These features can result in significant savings and increased conversion rates. 

Bcome.biz makes money by charging businesses for using its platform. The company claims that its platform can help businesses save up to 50% on impact costs and boost their conversion rates by up to 13%. It also claims that its platform can save businesses up to 80% of the time they would otherwise spend on sustainability tasks.

In summary, Bcome.biz is a sustainability platform for fashion businesses that helps them measure and improve their environmental, social, and economic impact, make data-driven decisions, and comply with sustainability regulations.

