Beryl''s business model is centered on building long-term partnerships with cities to deliver integrated and customized micro-mobility solutions. This approach allows the company to tailor its services to the specific needs of each community, ensuring a high level of service and user satisfaction. The company generates revenue through a combination of pay-per-ride fees, bundled minute packages, and day passes, offering flexibility to its users.

The company''s target market includes commuters, students, and tourists in urban areas who are looking for a convenient, affordable, and environmentally friendly way to travel. By providing a range of vehicle options, Beryl caters to a wide variety of user needs and preferences.

Beryl places a strong emphasis on safety, with all its vehicles designed to be robust and easy to use. The company also works closely with local authorities to ensure that its schemes are operated in a safe and responsible manner.

