The company’s flagship product is a Cellular Regeneration Unit (CRU) that employs a patented technology called Anionic Cellular Activation (ACA). This system is designed to turn a room into a regenerative environment by creating what the company calls an "antioxidant chamber". It operates continuously to purify the air of nanotoxic materials and emits bioavailable anions. According to the company, these anions are absorbed through the skin and lungs, helping to reduce oxidative stress and increase mitochondrial energy production (ATP). The technology is based on cold plasma medicine, which generates these therapeutic effects. Scientific research published in peer-reviewed journals, conducted in collaboration with research groups like cROS at the Health Research Institute of the Principality of Asturias (ISPA), supports claims that the device can increase cellular energy and reduce free radicals. The products are positioned as an anti-aging and performance-enhancing solution, with benefits including improved sleep quality, increased vitality, and better recovery times for athletes. 

Biow targets a diverse client base, from individuals seeking to improve their overall well-being and longevity to elite athletes and professional sports teams looking to enhance performance and recovery. The company has collaborated with organizations such as Real Madrid, the Spanish Football Federation, and Movistar Cycling. Initially focused on professional environments, Biow has since expanded its mission to make its technology accessible to the general public. The company, officially registered as BIOW EXPOSOMICS S.L.U., also emphasizes its commitment to international expansion, supported by programs aimed at promoting its products in key global markets. 
Keywords: cellular regeneration, oxidative stress reduction, cold plasma medicine, wellness technology, anionic cellular activation, mitochondrial energy, anti-aging device, air purification system, LOHAS & Wellness, biohacking, athletic performance, sleep improvement, preventive health, home wellness, cell therapy, ATP production, antioxidant, regenerative environment, sports technology, bioenergetics', '["Biotechnology","Venture Capital","BioTechnology","Subscription","Selling own inventory","online video platforms","DT and LS","Tech for Biotech and Pharma","Digital Care","Hard Tech","Breakout stage","audio-video-graphics","Manufacturing","Wellness Beauty","Longevity","Medical Devices","video players","science-based","Health","b2c","Deep Tech","Hardware","Health and Wellness"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 80.2, 4700, 1, 1, 24999990, NULL, NULL, -1268241, 2023, '[{"year":2022,"revenue":3204080,"ebitda":null,"profit":-530732,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":34},{"year":2023,"revenue":1348051,"ebitda":null,"profit":-1268241,"rnd":null,"valuation":24999990,"employees":35},{"year":2024,"revenue":1348051,"ebitda":null,"profit":-1268241,"rnd":null,"valuation":24999990,"employees":82},{"year":2025,"revenue":1348051,"ebitda":null,"profit":-1268241,"rnd":null,"valuation":24999990,"employees":96},{"year":2026,"revenue":1348051,"ebitda":null,"profit":-1268241,"rnd":null,"valuation":24999990,"employees":103}]', '2026-11-05T15:55:09.655Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:55:09.655Z');

