The company launched through the Entrepreneurs First accelerator program, initially as a chatbot on Facebook Messenger in the UK. After seeing rapid user adoption, Cleo entered the U.S. market in 2018 and shifted its focus entirely to this region. The platform operates on a freemium business model. The free version offers basic features like spending analysis, budget tracking, and bill reminders through its AI chatbot. Cleo''s AI communicates with a distinct, often humorous and sassy personality, offering features like "Roast Mode" to critique spending habits and "Hype Mode" to praise financial progress. 

Cleo generates revenue through tiered subscription plans that unlock advanced features. These premium tiers, such as Cleo Plus and Cleo Builder, provide services including interest-free cash advances up to $250, credit-building cards issued by WebBank, and enhanced financial insights. The Credit Builder Card is a secured card designed to help users establish or improve their credit scores. The company also earns interchange fees from transactions made with its card and fees from its cash advance service. Banking services are provided through a partnership with Thread Bank. 

Cleo has raised a total of approximately $175 million in funding over several rounds, with a Series C round of $80 million in 2022 led by Sofina. Other key investors include Balderton Capital, EQT Ventures, and LocalGlobe. The company was last valued at $500 million in 2022 and has demonstrated significant revenue growth, nearing profitability. Headquartered in London, Cleo has grown to a team of over 300 employees and has attracted millions of users, primarily in the United States. 

Keywords: AI financial assistant, personal finance, budgeting app, money management, chatbot, spending tracker, credit builder, cash advance, savings goals, fintech, Gen Z finance, financial health, AI money coach, expense tracking, overdraft protection, financial education, subscription model, transaction analysis, automated savings, credit score improvement', '["personalization","data management","social media marketing software","database","uk is8 financial services","software as a service","online community software","corporate learning management systems","accounting","human resource management system","ticket booking","hris management","Venture Capital","e-commerce platforms","web fonts","recruitment marketing","editors","visual and user generated content marketing","augmented reality","marketing","business process management","Core AI","SaaS","marketing automation","javascript graphics","customer relationship management","human resources","page builders","Angel","frameworks and libraries","loyalty and gamification","communication and collaboration","development","deployment","Banking","event management","content management system","Fintech","digital asset management","other advertising software","online video platforms","performance","marketing analytics","system analytics & monitoring","domain name services","marketing performance measurement","software development","payroll management and benefits administration","it infrastructure","web frameworks","source code management","open source","data warehousing","web platform extensions","unified communications","message boards","Artificial Intelligence","tag management","advanced analytics and data science","email","team collaboration","widgets","web servers","enterprise mobility management","software framework","customer service","content delivery network","programming languages","Challenger Bank","Verified Unicorns and $1B Exits","Commission","audio-video-graphics","advertising","infrastructure as a service","