Codat''s business model revolves around offering a more efficient and faster alternative to building and maintaining data integrations in-house. The company claims that its solutions can help industry leaders launch new integrations in weeks, not months, with lower maintenance requirements. Codat handles ongoing maintenance, optimizations, and edge-case fixes, allowing its clients to focus on delivering powerful products their customers love.

The company also offers tools for real-time reading, writing, and updating of data, and supports multiple client libraries and SDKs, enabling clients to build the best solution for their specific needs. Additionally, Codat provides an easy-to-build authorization system that allows customers to securely share all their data.

Codat''s revenue comes from the fees it charges for its services, which include automating data collection processes and making smarter risk decisions through easy access to customers'' financial data. The company prides itself on its secure infrastructure, built on industry-recognized SOC2 TSP and ISO27001 standards and AES-256 advanced data encryption.

In summary, Codat.io is a fintech startup that offers a faster, more efficient way for financial institutions and fintech companies to integrate and manage their data, particularly for underwriting and lending to small businesses.

