The company''s core offering is an automated code inspection and testing platform that analyzes C, C++, and Fortran source code to enhance performance, correctness, and security. This static analysis tool operates early in the development lifecycle, identifying issues without executing the code, thereby saving developer time and reducing costs. The platform is designed for sectors where performance is critical, such as high-performance computing, automotive, medical, renewable energy, and consumer electronics. The business model appears to be subscription-based, with different tiers available, including a free version, a professional plan, and a team plan, each offering escalating levels of features and support. Revenue is generated by providing these tools to corporate and institutional clients globally.

Codee''s platform provides deep code analysis to identify bugs, enforce coding standards, modernize legacy code, and address security vulnerabilities. A key feature is its ability to automatically fix detected issues, rewriting source code and adding annotations for CPU and GPU parallelization. The platform generates detailed reports that offer actionable insights for both developers and managers, helping to quantify technical debt and return on investment. By integrating into CI/CD workflows, Codee automates testing for every code change, which streamlines development and improves software quality. The company has secured approximately $7.29 million in funding over several rounds, with the latest being a Series A round in September 2023. This capital is being used to expand its customer base and further develop its platform to support more programming languages and hardware ecosystems like Arm and RISC-V.

Keywords: static code analysis, high-performance computing, code optimization, software modernization, C++, Fortran, parallel programming, DevSecOps, automated code inspection, software performance, compiler technologies, code correctness, legacy code, vulnerability detection, CI/CD integration, software development tools, GPU programming, multicore processing, embedded computing, code refactoring', '["High Performance Computing","Outside Tech","Venture Capital","online form builders","Big Data","editors","marketing","Subscription","SaaS","marketing automation","customer relationship management","communication and collaboration","development","Industry Innovation And Infrastructure (#9)","content management system","Dealflow Innovator","it infrastructure","source code management","open source","b2b","web platform extensions","customer service","Horizon Europe","Sustainable Cities And Communities (#11)","programming languages","customer self-service","website builders","virtualisation software","miscellaneous","Spinout","javascript libraries","wordpress plugins","Enterprise Software","analytics","devops","infrastructures as a service","security","Sustainable Development Goals","web analytics","data integration","platform as a service","Autonomous & Sensor Tech","consent management","Early stage","IoT InternetOfThings","configuration management","cookie compliance","containerization","Woman Founder","web tools and plugins"]', '["spinout","vc_backed","funded"]', 63.9, 7200, 0, 0, 20833325, -59582, 2020, -412859, 2024, '[{"year":2015,"revenue":44766,"ebitda":-14331,"profit":-18171,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":null},{"year":2016,"revenue":5578,"ebitda":-66376,"profit":-74811,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":null},{"year":2017,"revenue":23550,"ebitda":-58438,"profit":-74492,"rnd":null,"valuation":1999999,"employees":null},{"year":2018,"revenue":47585,"ebitda":-157143,"profit":-180745,"rnd":null,"valuation":1999999,"employees":null},{"year":2019,"revenue"