The company''s core service is a "Know Your Business" (KYB) tool designed to streamline customer onboarding. This platform automates the process of verifying a company''s identity, ownership structure, and business activities, which is crucial for compliance with Anti-Money Laundering (AML) regulations. By offering a single integration point for all business data, Condukt aims to help its clients, which include businesses in the payments and lending sectors, to reduce costs, simplify onboarding processes, and increase customer conversion rates. The platform addresses the inefficiencies and risks associated with manual verification methods and third-party services. Condukt operates as a data controller, collecting information from public sources like Companies House to provide its verification services. 

In April 2024, Condukt secured £2.5 million (approximately $3.18 million) in a pre-seed funding round. The round was backed by prominent venture capital firms including Lightspeed Venture Partners, Cocoa VC, Atomico, and Tiny VC. This funding supports the company''s efforts to scale its technology and expand its market share in the growing digital KYB sector. 

Keywords: business verification, Know Your Business, KYB, customer onboarding, data integration, B2B SaaS, regulatory compliance, Anti-Money Laundering, AML, fintech, risk management, identity verification, business data API, compliance automation, financial services software, regtech, London startup, Paulo Guichard, Bhasker Rao, Revolut alumni', '["database","Venture Capital","SaaS","Angel","deployment","software development","web frameworks","wikis","b2b","software framework","out of stealth","api management","programming languages","web & portal technology","programming","Enterprise Software","analytics","devops","issue trackers","operating systems & computing languages","application development & management","KYC","Early stage","ui frameworks","continuous integration"]', '["startup","rising_star","vc_backed","funded"]', 87.72, 420, 0, 0, 45454527, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:54:51.538Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:54:51.538Z');

The core of Consentio''s business is its smart e-commerce and social networking platform. This platform allows businesses to trade and communicate seamlessly, managing all transactions in one place. Unlike an open marketplace, Consentio is designed to enhance business relationships with existing partners, reducing competition and price wars that could destabilize the market.

Consentio''s business model is subscription-based, where clients pay for access to the platform and its various features. The company also offers additional services such as product catalog setup and activation of business counterparts, ensuring a smooth transition to digital operations.

By providing real-time analytics and a unified platform for trading and communication, Consentio aims to minimize food loss and create a healthier, more efficient industry. The company’s vision is to unite the fruits and vegetables community, making the supply chain more transparent and less wasteful.

