Crescenta''s business model is centered on democratizing access to an asset class that has traditionally been reserved for institutional investors. The company offers a curated selection of private equity funds, allowing investors to diversify their portfolios and potentially achieve higher returns than those offered by traditional investments. Crescenta also provides a software solution called Crescenta Alpha, which helps investors to consolidate, manage, and report on their investments.

The company makes money by charging a management fee on the assets it manages. This fee covers the costs of sourcing, due diligence, and managing the investments. Crescenta also offers a referral program, which rewards users for bringing new investors to the platform.

