The club''s business model revolves around competitive gaming, content creation, and strategic partnerships. DUX fields professional teams in titles such as EA SPORTS FC and NBA 2K. A pivotal moment in its history was the 2020 acquisition of a stake in the professional football club Internacional de Madrid, rebranding it as DUX Internacional de Madrid. This move was a first for an esports organization and solidified its strategy of blending the virtual and real sports worlds. The club has since expanded its physical sports presence by partnering with the women''s first division team EDF Logroño (now DUX Logroño). Revenue is generated through sponsorships, with partners like Adidas and MediaMarkt, and the creation of digital content. The company has also ventured into talent representation and strategic consulting. 

DUX Gaming has attracted high-profile investors, including professional footballers Thibaut Courtois and Borja Iglesias, and NBA champion Marc Gasol. These investors also serve as ambassadors, enhancing the club''s credibility and reach. In October 2022, DUX secured a €3 million funding round led by Marc Gasol to fuel its international expansion, particularly in Latin America, and to develop new business lines. This expansion included moving its NBA 2K League franchise, DUX Infinitos, to Mexico City. The company is led by CEO Mario Fernández, a former executive from EA Sports, and recently appointed Jorge Huguet, formerly of Sony Interactive Entertainment, as Corporate President to guide further growth. In early 2024, DUX diversified into the fitness sector by acquiring a majority stake in the online training company Volava. 

Keywords: esports club, sports simulation gaming, content creation, professional gaming, EA SPORTS FC, NBA 2K, DUX Internacional de Madrid, DUX Logroño, athlete investors, virtual sports, traditional sports, esports talent agency, digital content, sports marketing, gaming entertainment, football esports, basketball esports, Latin America esports, VIZZ Agency, Mario Fernández, Jordi Torras, Xavier Robles, Thibaut Courtois, Borja Iglesias, Marc Gasol', '["Venture Capital","Advertising","SaaS","Angel","it infrastructure","web frameworks","b2b","web servers","software framework","web and application servers","javascript libraries","Gaming","eSports","b2c","Early stage","ui frameworks"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 62.38, 2100, 0, 0, 14999994, NULL, NULL, -406767, 2023, '[{"year":2022,"revenue":458050,"ebitda":null,"profit":-568133,"rnd":null,"valuation":14999994,"employees":19},{"year":2023,"revenue":507619,"ebitda":null,"profit":-406767,"rnd":null,"valuation":14999994,"employees":17},{"year":2024,"revenue":507619,"ebitda":null,"profit":-406767,"rnd":null,"valuation":14999994,"employees":18},{"year":2025,"revenue":507619,"ebitda":null,"profit":-406767,"rnd":null,"valuation":14999994,"employees":19},{"year":2026,"revenue":507619,"ebitda":null,"profit":-406767,"rnd":null,"valuation":14999994,"employees":19}]', '2026-11-05T15:56:04.243Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:56:04.243Z');

The company''s first product, launched in 2020, was the world''s first CBD-infused tampon, designed to provide localized relief from menstrual cramps. Building on this, Daye introduced a tampon-based at-home screening kit. This platform enables users to test for disruptions in the vaginal microbiome, which can indicate susceptibility to infections like bacterial vaginosis (BV) and yeast infections. The service has expanded to include screening for STIs such as chlamydia, gonorrhoea, and trichomonas, as well as HPV, using PCR technology for analysis in accredited labs. The business model operates on a direct-to-consumer basis, selling products like organic tampons, diagnostic kits, and supplements via its website, with options for monthly subscriptions. The company also provides personalized aftercare, including prescription treatments and consultations with healthcare specialists. 

Daye has raised approximately $18.6 million (£14 million) in funding through several rounds, including a Series A round of £10 million ($11.5 million) in October 2022. Key investors include Hambro Perks, MassMutual Ventures, Khosla Ventures, and Index Ventures. The company is preparing for expansion into the U.S. market and aims to develop a comprehensive digital health platform covering conditions like PCOS and endometriosis. 

