The core of Dersu''s business is a mobile application designed for outdoor enthusiasts, particularly those interested in hiking and trekking. The platform operates on a subscription-based model, providing users access to a curated library of mountain routes created by professionals. A key feature of the service is its ability to personalize route recommendations based on a user''s declared fitness and technical skill level. This aims to ensure that individuals undertake challenges appropriate for their capabilities, thereby increasing safety. The app provides detailed information for each route, including difficulty ratings, complex sections, necessary equipment, and weather conditions. 

In May 2022, Dersu secured €1 million in a seed funding round. The investment was led by several venture capital funds, including KFund, Itnig, Didi Value Partners, and Extensión Fund, with participation from various angel investors. This capital injection was earmarked for expanding the inventory of available routes, enriching the platform''s educational content, and developing community-building features to connect users with each other and with mountain professionals. Additionally, the company initiated a new data-focused venture, Dersu Data, in collaboration with ITAINNOVA, to analyze information on mountain activities to improve strategic planning in safety, sustainability, and tourism. 

Keywords: mountain safety, hiking app, route planning, outdoor activities, trekking, mountaineering, sustainable tourism, digital guide, GPS maps, trail recommendations, outdoor community, weather conditions, equipment list, skill level matching, professional routes, Dersu Data, Borja Delgado, Fernando Errekalde, Juan Delgado, María Renilla', '["Venture Capital","Subscription","SaaS","Travel","b2c","Early stage","Mobile app","Woman Founder","Travel Analytics & Software"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 57.16, 1900, 0, 0, 4999998, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"year":2022,"revenue":738636,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":4999998,"employees":13},{"year":2023,"revenue":795454,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":4999998,"employees":16},{"year":2024,"revenue":795454,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":4999998,"employees":14},{"year":2025,"revenue":795454,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":4999998,"employees":16},{"year":2026,"revenue":795454,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":4999998,"employees":15}]', '2026-11-05T15:56:04.243Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:56:04.243Z');

The company''s core offering is the DexoryView platform, which launched commercially in January 2023. This platform utilizes autonomous mobile robots (AMRs) to scan warehouses, capturing high-definition 3D scans, images, and data from barcodes and labels. These robots, noted as being the world''s tallest at up to 12-14 meters, can scan over 10,000 pallet locations per hour. The collected data is used to create a real-time digital twin of the warehouse, providing complete visibility of inventory, space utilization, and operations. The AI-powered platform analyzes this data to identify inventory discrepancies, optimize storage space, track assets, and monitor environmental conditions. This helps clients increase inventory accuracy, improve fulfillment rates, and enhance operational efficiency. 

Dexory operates on a subscription-based Robotics as a Service (RaaS) and Software as a Service (SaaS) model, which includes the robots, platform access, and servicing. Its client base spans third-party logistics (3PLs), manufacturing, automotive, e-commerce, and aviation, with customers including Maersk, GXO, DB Schenker, Unipart, and GE Appliances. Headquartered in the UK, Dexory has expanded its operations into North America, opening a headquarters in Nashville, Tennessee. The company has raised a total of $120 million, including a $80 million Series B round in late 2024 to fuel its global expansion and AI development. 

Keywords: warehouse automation, robotics, artificial intelligence, digital twin, supply chain management, logistics technology, inventory management, autonomous mobile robots, data intelligence, warehouse visibility, real-time data, inventory accuracy, space optimization, SaaS, RaaS, warehouse operations, logistics automation, supply chain optimization, inventory scanning, pallet racking, asset tracking, data analytics, 3PL solutions, manufacturing logistics, warehouse efficiency', '["accelerator","data management","social media marketing software","database","software as a service","sales","Logistics and Delivery","human resource management system","user onboarding","Inventory","Venture Capital","operations","editors","ad exchanges","visual and user generated content marketing","marketing","mobile application development platforms","Core AI","Subscription","SaaS","sales enablement","marketing automation","javascript graphics","customer relationship management","human resources","page builders","Angel","frameworks and libraries","communication and collaboration","development","deployment","identity and access management","Warehouse Automation","testing and qa","content management system","UKis Digital and technologies","marketing analytics","risk and compliance","marketing performance measurement","software development","DT and LS","it infrastructure","web frameworks","Logistics Robots","Inventory Management","database management","b2b","web platform extensions","Artificial Intelligence","Robotics","email","it","team collaboration","widgets","Horizon Europe","programming languages","social media analytics and monitoring","Commission","audio-video-graphics","advertising","human resource","Manufacturing","website builders","enterprise resource planning","site search","miscellaneous","programming","network security","Supply Chain Management","AI Applications","cloud infrastructure computing","business intelligence","governance-risk and compliance","account-based market