Elvie''s primary market is women, particularly mothers or those planning to become mothers. The company''s products are designed to be user-friendly, with a focus on home use. The Elvie Pump, for instance, is a smart breast pump that allows mothers to manage their breastfeeding routine without any hassle. The company also offers the Elvie Trainer, a device that uses biofeedback to guide users through Kegel exercises, helping them strengthen their pelvic floor muscles.

Elvie operates on a direct-to-consumer business model, selling its products through its website. The company also has a referral program, where existing customers can refer friends and receive an Amazon gift card as a reward. Some of Elvie''s products may also be covered by insurance, offering customers up to 40% savings.

Elvie''s revenue comes from the sale of its products. The company also potentially earns from partnerships with insurance companies, although the specifics of these arrangements are not publicly disclosed.

