The company was established in Spain in 1991, opening its first office and a physical point of sale in Madrid. In 2004, Equinvest expanded its operations to Portugal by opening a new branch in Lisbon. A significant milestone occurred in 2015 when the company moved its official headquarters to Villaviciosa de Odón (Madrid) and opened a second sales location. In April 2024, the private equity fund Nzyme acquired a significant stake in Equinvest, aiming to drive technological transformation and international expansion. The company''s management team includes Javier Póveda as CEO and a directive team of five partners: Fernando Díaz Solís, Vicente Vazquez Bouza, Jose Manuel Gasalla, Juan López Santamaría, and Pablo Campos. 

Operating in the niche market of equine health, Equinvest has established itself through a commitment to quality and specialized knowledge, with a team that includes veterinarians and pharmacists. The company generates revenue, reported to be over €5 million, through the sale of its extensive catalog of over 4,000 products. Clients can purchase goods via multiple channels, including telephone, email, an online platform, and at their physical locations. 

