The core of Frenetic''s business is a web-based software-as-a-service (SaaS) platform that leverages artificial intelligence to automate and optimize the design of magnetic components. This platform allows electrical engineers to input their specifications and, within seconds, receive a range of design options, complete with simulations and component suggestions from various manufacturers. The business model is twofold: it generates revenue from subscriptions to its design and simulation software, and it also offers a manufacturing service. This service manages the entire supply chain, from prototyping and sampling to mass production of the custom-designed magnetic components, providing a comprehensive solution from concept to finished product. Frenetic serves clients across various industries, including electric vehicles, renewable energy, and industrial applications, who require high-performance, custom magnetic solutions. The company has secured significant funding, including a €10 million round in 2023, to fuel its expansion, particularly in the United States market, and to further develop its AI technology. 

The service streamlines a traditionally complex and time-consuming process, which often relies on estimations and iterative physical prototyping. By employing physics-based models and machine learning algorithms, Frenetic''s platform delivers highly accurate designs and performance predictions without the need for initial physical samples. A key feature is the platform''s ability to provide instant feedback on the feasibility and performance of a design, allowing for rapid iteration. The company''s unique selling proposition lies in its integration of an advanced design tool with a managed manufacturing service, effectively creating an end-to-end ecosystem for custom magnetics that reduces design time from weeks to mere hours and accelerates the delivery of physical prototypes. 

