The company''s business model is subscription-based, with revenue generated from monthly or annual fees. Pricing tiers, starting from around $44-$60 per month, are structured to cater to different organizational needs, from small teams to large enterprises. Geckoboard serves a wide range of clients across industries like marketing, sales, and operations who require a simplified way to monitor business metrics. The platform is designed for non-technical users, allowing anyone to build and share dashboards without coding knowledge. This focus on simplicity and accessibility aims to embed data into the daily culture and decision-making processes of its client companies. 

Geckoboard''s core product is a customizable dashboard that aggregates and visualizes data from over 90 third-party business tools, including Google Analytics, Salesforce, Zendesk, and Google Sheets. Its main function is to transform complex data into clear, easily understandable visualizations that update in real-time. Key features include a drag-and-drop dashboard creator, optimizations for displaying dashboards on large TV screens, and various sharing options like link sharing, snapshots for Slack and email, and mobile-friendly access. The platform helps teams track progress against goals, respond quickly to performance changes, and maintain alignment by providing a single, consolidated view of essential metrics. The company has secured backing from notable investors such as Index Ventures, DN Capital, Point Nine, and 500 Startups, raising a total of approximately $4.12 million across several funding rounds. 

