The company''s history includes a significant strategic move in early 2017 when it merged with GetYourHero. GetYourHero, also founded in Barcelona in 2014 by Henrik Beckmann and Sebastian Janus, specialized in cleaning services as well. Prior to the merger, in October 2015, GetYourHero had acquired the Spanish assets of competitor Helpling, while selling its French operations to them, in a move to consolidate its position in the Spanish market. Following the merger with Clintu, the two brands continued to operate independently for a time, with Clintu focusing on the residential cleaning market and GetYourHero targeting the office cleaning sector. Alex Espel took the lead of the combined entity. 

Clintu''s business model is centered on its web and mobile applications, which allow both individual and business clients to book services online. The company earns revenue by taking a commission on the services managed through its platform. Users can select the specific service they need, choose a convenient day and time, and book professionals who have been previously vetted. The platform offers flexibility, allowing for modifications or cancellations up to 24 hours in advance. For businesses, Clintu provides a consolidated monthly invoice for all services rendered. Payments can be made through various methods including credit card, PayPal, and bank transfer. 

The company has secured funding to fuel its growth, raising a total of $1.35 million over two rounds. A seed round in 2015 brought in $113K, followed by a Series A round in January 2018 for $1.24 million, led by Dozen. Other investors include Seaya and Media Digital Ventures. Keywords: home services, office cleaning, online marketplace, domestic services, cleaning booking app, professional cleaners, handyman services, moving services, home renovation platform, on-demand services, Barcelona startup, Alex Espel Ribera, Clintu, GetYourHero, home maintenance, facility services, residential cleaning, commercial cleaning, service marketplace, plumbing services, painting services', '["Real Estate","help desk software","Venture Capital","Online Booking","Booking","development","Cleaning Services","it infrastructure","help desk management","On-Demand Services","web servers","customer service","App","programming languages","Commission","Breakout stage","Sharing Economy","web and application servers","Home Living","javascript libraries","Peer-to-Peer","analytics","Directory","b2c","Marketplace & ecommerce","live chat","blogs","ui frameworks","Real Estate Services","Cleaning","On-Demand"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 85.51, 890, 0, 0, 7499997, -564900, 2015, -582547, 2015, '[{"year":2015,"revenue":48124,"ebitda":-564900,"profit":-582547,"rnd":null,"valuation":7499997,"employees":null},{"year":2016,"revenue":48124,"ebitda":-564900,"profit":-582547,"rnd":null,"valuation":7499997,"employees":null},{"year":2017,"revenue":48124,"ebitda":-564900,"profit":-582547,"rnd":null,"valuation":7499997,"employees":null},{"year":2018,"revenue":1893939,"ebitda":-564900,"profit":-582547,"rnd":null,"valuation":7499997,"employees":29},{"year":2019,"revenue":2272726,"ebitda":-564900,"profit":-582547,"rnd":null,"valuation":7499997,"employees":32},{"year":2020,"revenue":2499999,"ebitda":-564900,"profit":-582547,"rnd":null,"valuation":7499997,"employees":36},{"year":2021,"revenue":2727272,"ebi