Initially, Graphy developed a comprehensive product covering the entire data value chain, from ingestion and modeling to analysis and visualization. However, this complex solution struggled to gain user engagement. This led to a strategic pivot towards a leaner product, "Graphy Lite," which focused on solving one core problem: creating visually appealing charts quickly. This shift proved successful, resulting in significant user growth, reaching 50,000 users within ten months of enabling account creation. 

The company''s core offering is a no-code, AI-powered platform that enables users to transform data into interactive charts and dashboards. The service is built for a professional clientele including marketing managers, data analysts, and founders who need to present data insights for business reports or investor updates. The platform features one-click data import from sources like Google Analytics, HubSpot, and spreadsheets, aiming to eliminate the need for complex technical integrations. Users can customize visualizations and embed the interactive charts into platforms such as Notion and Slack for broader communication. 

Graphy''s business model is freemium, allowing anyone to create a limited number of charts for free, which includes a Graphy watermark. Revenue is generated through an upgraded subscription plan that removes the branding, allows for custom brand colors, and unlocks additional features. The platform also offers an SDK and Embed APIs for businesses wanting to integrate the data storytelling capabilities directly into their own products. 

Keywords: data visualization, no-code analytics, interactive charts, data storytelling, business intelligence dashboards, Andrey Vinitsky, data reporting, freemium SaaS, data analysis tool, dashboard collaboration, chart maker, Notion integration, Slack integration, AI data insights, marketing analytics, financial data visualization, startup analytics, embeddable charts, Graphy.app, data communication', '["database","Team Collaboration","Venture Capital","recruitment marketing","ad exchanges","Productivity Tools","Subscription","SaaS","Angel","performance","system analytics & monitoring","web frameworks","SaaS","database management","b2b","web servers","App","audio-video-graphics","advertising","miscellaneous","cloud infrastructure computing","Analytics","javascript libraries","Enterprise Software","analytics","other audio-video-graphics software","devops","Interactive Dashboard","security","issue trackers","web analytics","application development & management","Early stage","applicant tracking systems","charting","Remote Job","configuration management","Collaboration","captcha","web tools and plugins"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 75.65, 110000, 0, 0, 36363622, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"year":2019,"revenue":681818,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":36363622,"employees":13},{"year":2020,"revenue":1022727,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":36363622,"employees":21},{"year":2021,"revenue":1893939,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":36363622,"employees":31},{"year":2022,"revenue":2272726,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":36363622,"employees":17},{"year":2023,"revenue":2272726,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":36363622,"employees":33},{"year":2024,"revenue":2272726,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":36363622,"employees":29},{"year":2025,"revenue":2272726,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":36363622,"employees":34},{"year":2026,"revenue":2272726,"ebit