Founded in October 2025 by CEO Pablo Molina and President Iñaki Berenguer, the former leadership team of the insurance technology company CoverWallet, InfiniteWatch operates from New York and Madrid. The founders'' experience scaling CoverWallet, which was later acquired by Aon, informed their vision to address the lack of transparency in the growing use of AI agents for customer engagement. The company''s platform serves as an observability layer for AI-mediated customer interactions across web and voice channels, analyzing over two million interactions per month for its clients in the financial services, e-commerce, and healthcare sectors. 

The company''s business model is centered on providing tools that offer real-time visibility into user experience, compliance, performance, and revenue leakage. The platform features two main products: the Session Replay Agent and the Voice Agent. The Session Replay Agent automatically analyzes web sessions to identify user experience issues that impact conversion rates. The Voice Agent deploys synthetic personas to test voice AI systems at scale, identify quality issues, and monitor calls for performance and compliance insights. Unlike traditional analytics tools, InfiniteWatch integrates monitoring and deployment, aiming to predict issues before they happen. The company plans to expand its offerings in 2026 to include a Messaging Agent, Email Agent, and AI Co-Browsing capabilities. 

Keywords: customer interaction intelligence, AI observability, agentic AI, session replay, voice analytics, user experience, conversion optimization, compliance monitoring, predictive analytics, AI agent testing, revenue leakage, financial services technology, e-commerce technology, healthcare technology, Pablo Molina, Iñaki Berenguer, Base10 Partners', '["data management","data security","Venture Capital","MLops","Subscription","SaaS","marketing automation","page builders","Angel","frameworks and libraries","development","testing and qa","AI Data Preparation and Generation","web frameworks","b2b","Artificial Intelligence","genAI Operation Layer","web servers","software framework","out of stealth","programming languages","infrastructure as a service","web & portal technology","programming","cloud infrastructure computing","javascript libraries","Enterprise Software","analytics","operating systems & computing languages","cloud hosting","platform as a service","javascript frameworks","consent management","Early stage","big data processing","ui frameworks","charting","email marketing","web tools and plugins"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 68.26, 600, 1, 1, 18181811, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:53:55.756Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:53:55.756Z');

The company operates in the K-12 education market, directly serving schools and teachers. Its business model is based on providing a comprehensive curricular proposal that includes a wide array of resources. These resources range from manipulable materials for hands-on learning to digital platforms featuring interactive activities and games, complemented by detailed teacher training and support. Revenue is generated through subscriptions or licensing fees paid by educational institutions for access to this integrated system. 

Innovamat''s core offering is a structured pedagogical program that guides students through mathematical concepts in a scaffolded manner, starting with concrete manipulation, moving to pictorial representation, and finally to abstract symbols. The platform provides personalized learning paths, allowing students to progress at their own pace while enabling teachers to monitor progress and identify areas where intervention is needed. A key differentiator is its focus on problem-solving and critical thinking rather than rote learning, aiming to build a solid and lasting understanding of mathematics. The company has achieved significant milestones, including rapid expansion into various regions of Spain and entry into international markets such as Italy and several Latin American countries, serving thousands of schools and hundreds of thousands of students. 

