The platform serves prospective home buyers by providing a more intuitive and detailed property search experience. Unlike traditional property portals that primarily serve estate agents, Jitty focuses on the buyer''s journey and does not charge agents for listings or leads. Its business model centers on creating a comprehensive, user-friendly tool for buyers, with plans to introduce monetization strategies as it scales. The company has successfully raised a total of $5.8 million in funding over two rounds, with a pre-seed round of $2 million in 2023 and a subsequent seed round of $3.8 million in August 2025, led by REA Group. Notable investors include Google''s AI-focused fund Gradient Ventures, Sequoia Capital, and Atomico. 

Jitty''s core product is a property search engine that utilizes artificial intelligence, including large language models (LLMs) and computer vision, to analyze and extract detailed information from property listings. The technology can interpret photos, floor plans, and descriptions to identify features that are often not available in standard search filters, such as ''open-plan kitchens'', ''Victorian fireplaces'', or ''renovation potential''. Users can perform highly specific, natural language searches, combining criteria like commute times to specific locations, property aesthetics, and room sizes. The platform also provides collaborative tools that allow users to create shortlists, add notes, and share properties with family and friends, moving the process away from disorganized spreadsheets and messaging apps. Jitty aims to provide complete market coverage and has already facilitated over 250,000 property searches since its launch. 

Keywords: property search engine, AI home search, real estate technology, proptech, UK property market, home buying platform, natural language search, computer vision, residential property, collaborative property search, real estate data, property listing aggregator, mortgage process, floor plan analysis, commuter-based search, property investment tools, digital home buying, London startup, venture capital, real estate AI', '["database","Real Estate","photo galleries","Venture Capital","SaaS","marketing automation","human resources","Angel","content management system","performance","web frameworks","customer data platforms","Artificial Intelligence","software framework","content delivery network","programming languages","website builders","javascript libraries","Real Estate Software","analytics","web analytics","b2c","Early stage","blogs","applicant tracking systems","healthcare marketing","ui frameworks"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 59.47, 200000, 0, 0, 17272720, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:54:51.538Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:54:51.538Z');

Jobandtalent’s end-to-end digital platform automates key steps in hiring, from candidate sourcing and screening to onboarding and payroll management. This data-driven approach enables rapid placement—crucial in high-volume, deskless job markets—while maintaining consistent quality and fairness in candidate evaluation. By integrating with applicant tracking systems and offering a mobile-first experience, Jobandtalent supports flexible, reliable employment opportunities and agile workforce management for businesses.

The company has achieved significant scale, placing over 340,000 workers in more than 2,500 companies in 2022, and operates in at least 10 countries across Europe, the US, and Latin America. Backed by prominent investors and recognized as one of Spain’s highest-valued unicorns, Jobandtalent continues to expand its reach and technological capabilities to redefine the future of temporary work.

