 The firm has secured significant financial backing, raising a total of $25.2 million over five funding rounds. Key investors include Atomico, Nesta Impact Investments, Forward Partners, and several angel investors like Michael Pennington, the co-founder of Gumtree. The funding has been instrumental in scaling operations, expanding its service offerings, and enhancing its technology platform. 

 Koru Kids'' primary business is a technology-enabled marketplace connecting families with childcare providers. The business model is multifaceted, initially focusing on an after-school service that matches parents with vetted and trained student nannies. It has since expanded to include nanny shares, where two families can share one nanny, making costs more manageable, and a "home nursery" model that supports educators in setting up small childcare businesses in their homes. This addresses different segments of the childcare market, from after-school hours for school-aged children to full-day care for babies and toddlers. The company generates revenue by managing the entire administrative process for families, including recruitment, vetting, contracts, payroll, and pension setup, for a fee. This full-stack approach aims to provide a seamless experience for working parents. 

 The service platform is a key feature, automating much of the matching and administrative work. For parents, it offers a streamlined way to find vetted providers, with Koru Kids stating they accept only a small percentage of applicants to maintain quality. For nannies and childminders, the company provides training in first aid, educational philosophies, and ongoing support through a community network. This dual focus on supporting both families and childcare professionals is central to their mission of creating a new, more effective childcare system. Keywords: childcare platform, after-school nannies, nanny sharing, home nursery, childminder services, London childcare, parent support, student nannies, nanny payroll, childcare administration, early years education, flexible childcare, working parents support, Rachel Carrell, childcare marketplace, vetting nannies, nanny training, family services, childcare technology, UK childcare', '["accelerator","social media marketing software","database","online community software","sales","corporate learning management systems","recurring billing","payments","accounting","chat","Reduced Inequalities (#10)","hr","hris management","Venture Capital","recruitment marketing","Jobs Recruitment","payroll","editors","ad exchanges","visual and user generated content marketing","marketing","marketing automation","javascript graphics","customer relationship management","human resources","page builders","Angel","frameworks and libraries","communication and collaboration","development","content management system","digital asset management","other advertising software","enterprise","marketing analytics","Children","marketing performance measurement","payroll management and benefits administration","it infrastructure","web frameworks","source code management","open source","web platform extensions","tag management","email","team collaboration","widgets","web servers","human resource management","search engines","customer service","content d