Latitude''s primary clients are businesses that rely heavily on data to drive their decisions. These include sectors like finance, healthcare, retail, and technology, where data-driven insights are crucial for strategic planning and operational efficiency. The platform is designed to reduce the back-and-forth typically associated with data analysis, speeding up feedback loops and empowering true self-service for users.

The core of Latitude''s offering is its hybrid canvas, a real-time, multiplayer environment where data experts and stakeholders can work together seamlessly. This canvas allows experts to run SQL queries while enabling non-technical users to tweak these queries or create their own using a visual builder. This dual approach ensures that both technical and non-technical users can collaborate effectively, making data exploration faster and more intuitive.

Latitude makes money through a subscription-based business model. Clients pay for access to the platform, which includes features like the visual builder, real-time collaboration tools, and advanced data visualization capabilities. Additional revenue streams may include premium features, custom integrations, and dedicated support services.

In summary, Latitude is revolutionizing the way businesses interact with their data by fostering a collaborative environment that bridges the gap between data teams and decision-makers. This approach not only accelerates the data analysis process but also makes it more inclusive and efficient.

