The business functions as a two-sided marketplace, funding loans not from its own balance sheet but with capital from institutional investors like pension funds and hedge funds. This structure allows Lendable to offer unsecured personal loans to a broad spectrum of UK residents, including those who might be underserved by prime lenders. Revenue is primarily generated from the interest on these loans and a one-off loan fee that is added to the principal. The company generates new loan applications by partnering with price comparison websites and retailers. Lendable became profitable in 2017 and achieved unicorn status in early 2021 after a secondary share sale valued it over £1 billion. A subsequent funding round in March 2022, led by the Ontario Teachers'' Pension Plan Board, elevated its valuation to approximately £3.5 billion. 

Lendable''s core offering consists of unsecured personal loans ranging from £1,000 to £25,000, with repayment terms of one to five years. The entire process is digital, from application to funding, leveraging artificial intelligence and machine learning for credit assessment. This technology enables the platform to analyze extensive data points beyond traditional credit scores, facilitating instant loan decisions and rapid fund disbursement, often within hours. The company also offers an eligibility check that doesn''t impact an applicant''s credit score. Beyond personal loans, Lendable has expanded its product suite to include car finance through its Autolend brand and credit cards and loans via its Zable brand, which also operates in the United States. 

Keywords: consumer finance, personal loans, fintech, online lending, credit automation, institutional investors, marketplace lending, debt consolidation, car finance, credit cards, AI credit scoring, digital loans, unsecured loans, Zable, Autolend, Martin Kissinger, alternative lending, consumer credit, loan platform, financial technology', '["corporate","data management","social media marketing software","database","uk is8 financial services","data security","corporate learning management systems","Private Equity","accounting","help desk software","human resource management system","Venture Capital","web fonts","recruitment marketing","editors","augmented reality","marketing","javascript graphics","human resources","page builders","Angel","frameworks and libraries","communication and collaboration","development","identity and access management","testing and qa","content management system","Consumer Lending","Fintech","other advertising software","job board software","system analytics & monitoring","software development","payroll management and benefits administration","it infrastructure","web frameworks","source code management","open source","database management","data warehousing","b2b","tag management","advanced analytics and data science","it infrastructure & operations management","it","team collaboration","widgets","web servers","search marketing","enterprise mobility management","software framework","online review management","customer service","threat intelligence","programming languages","documentation tools","Verified Unicorns and $1B Exits","Commission","audio-video-graphics","advertising","payment processing","human resource","error and exception monitoring","web & portal technology","generative ai","web and application servers","miscellaneous","programming","cloud infrastructure computing","business intelligence","governance-risk and compliance","office suites","dev tools","javascript libraries","Verified Thoroughbreds","intelligence and analytics","cu