The company''s business model is centered around its digital platform, accessible via a website and mobile app, which streamlines the process of staff management and recruitment. For healthcare centers, Livo offers solutions to manage both internal and external staff, including tools for posting job openings and selecting candidates. This helps facilities eliminate scattered communications like calls and emails by centralizing everything on one platform, aiming to increase efficiency and ensure uninterrupted patient care. For healthcare professionals, the platform provides a flexible way to find and apply for work that fits their schedules and preferences, offering transparency and autonomy. Livo generates revenue through commissions on bookings made via its platform. 

The company has received seed funding, including an investment from Techstars in 2021. Livo also made a strategic move in April 2025 by acquiring Cam Health, a Barcelona-based company in the clinics and outpatient services industry. 

