Initially launched as a marketplace model, Mascoteros connected a network of over 300 pet shops and 360 vendors with pet owners, offering a catalog of more than 42,000 items. This model focused on digitalizing sales for small and medium-sized businesses, particularly veterinary clinics, taking a commission on each transaction. Following a strategy shift, the company transitioned into a direct-to-consumer online store. This change included the introduction of its own product lines to complement third-party brands. The company now manages three distinct in-house brands: Nativo for natural pet food, Taniwa for vegan cosmetics, and Animal Republic for toys and accessories. 

Mascoteros has secured funding from notable investors including Antai Venture Builder, Atresmedia, Kibo Ventures, and through platforms like Crowdcube. A significant funding round in 2020 raised €1 million to consolidate growth and expand its service offerings. Beyond e-commerce, the company provides services such as remote veterinary consultations and facilitates support for animal shelters. The business also operates the Mascoteros Foundation, which provides veterinary resources and support to animal protection agencies. 

