Mimo''s business model revolves around offering a software-as-a-service (SaaS) platform. This means they provide their software over the internet, and businesses pay a subscription fee to use it. The platform leverages insights and flexible financing options to help businesses understand and manage their cash flow better. By doing so, Mimo aims to reduce the risk of small business failures due to cash flow issues.

The company is currently in a limited beta phase, meaning they are testing their product with a select group of users before a full launch. Interested businesses can join a waiting list to gain access to the platform. Mimo''s ultimate goal is to enable entrepreneurs to focus on growing their businesses without the stress of financial management.

In summary, Mimo is a fintech startup that simplifies B2B transactions for SMBs through an automated, easy-to-use platform. They make money by charging subscription fees for their SaaS product, which helps businesses manage cash flow and reduce administrative burdens.

