The core of Minube''s service is a web and mobile application that aggregates recommendations from a community of over 1.5 million travelers. Users can discover new vacation ideas through an "Inspiration" tool that filters destinations by criteria like trip type, distance, or even color. The platform hosts a vast database of tourist attractions, restaurants, and hotels, allowing users to build personalized, downloadable, and offline-accessible travel guides. A key feature is its ability to automatically create photo galleries of users'' trips by detecting GPS data from their phone''s camera, organizing photos by location and date to create a shareable travel album.

The business model centers on experiential marketing for destinations, accommodations, and attractions, as well as booking commissions. Since a 2019 update, users can directly book thousands of tours, activities, and day trips through the app. Minube provides content creation and promotion services for businesses within the travel sector, enabling them to connect with travelers who are actively planning trips. The company has secured $4.38 million in funding over four rounds, with the latest being a Series A round in December 2018.

