The process for sellers involves entering their car''s registration number and mileage on the Motorway website to receive an instant estimated valuation. If the seller is happy with the valuation, they can create a car profile by taking photos and answering a few questions about the vehicle''s condition. The car is then entered into a daily online sale where over 5,000 verified dealers can make offers.

At the end of the sale, the highest offer is presented to the seller, who can choose to accept or decline it. If the offer is accepted, the winning dealer will arrange to collect the car from the seller''s home and make payment via bank transfer. Motorway''s service is free for private car sellers, with the company making its revenue by charging a commission fee to the purchasing dealer.

