Sutton''s journey in the industry began in South Africa, where he gained knowledge in various categories, from diamonds to branded chains. He later started his own diamond wholesale business before launching an online bridal jewelry retail business in the UK. It was during this time that he identified the significant operational burdens. He met Andre Woons after being accepted into the Entrepreneur First program, a startup incubator, and together they launched Nivoda to address these challenges. 

The platform connects jewelry retailers with a global network of suppliers, offering an extensive inventory of natural diamonds, lab-grown diamonds, colored gemstones, and melee diamonds. Nivoda''s business model centers on simplifying procurement for jewelers. It allows them to purchase from multiple suppliers in a single transaction and receive one consolidated invoice in their local currency. The company manages the entire fulfillment process, including quality control, logistics, customs, and paperwork, delivering stones directly to the jeweler''s store. This centralized approach is designed to reduce operational costs and inventory risk for retailers. 

Nivoda serves a global client base, with customers in over 60 countries. The platform offers several digital tools to enhance the user experience, including API feeds and a Shopify plugin for e-commerce integration, and a white-label virtual showroom for in-store sales. The company also provides flexible payment and credit solutions to its customers. Since its inception, Nivoda has seen significant growth, marked by substantial funding rounds, including a $30 million Series B and a $51 million Series C in 2024. The company has expanded its offerings from diamonds to include colored gemstones and plans to introduce finished jewelry. 

Keywords: B2B marketplace, diamond trade, gemstone sourcing, jewelry procurement, online diamond marketplace, lab-grown diamonds, jewelry supply chain, David Sutton, Andre Woons, jewelry logistics, e-commerce integration, virtual showroom, diamond wholesale, colored gemstones, melee diamonds, jewelry retailers, diamond suppliers, fintech, jewelry industry, global diamond network', '["database","software as a service","accounting","Fashion","Luxury","Venture Capital","e-commerce platforms","web fonts","editors","marketing","customer relationship management","frameworks and libraries","communication and collaboration","content management system","enterprise","software development","payroll management and benefits administration","it infrastructure","web frameworks","wikis","uk is8 creative industries","b2b","tag management","team collaboration","search engines","software framework","content delivery network","programming languages","Commission","Breakout stage","audio-video-graphics","payment processing","enterprise resource planning","B2b Online Marketplace","miscellaneous","programming","e-commerce","javascript libraries","intelligence and analytics","analytics","devops","issue trackers","operating systems & computing languages","web analytics","platform as a service","application development & management","javascript frameworks","Diamond","Marketplace & ecommerce","font scripts","Luxury","blogs","design","ui frameworks","accounting and finance","email marketing","continuous integration","captcha","web tools and plugins","web hosting"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 64.47, 170000, 0, 0, 231818089, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"year":2019,"revenue":361363,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":12},{"year":2020,"revenue":992424,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":24},{"year":2021,"revenue":2575757,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":60},{"year":2022,"revenue":53658312,"eb