Nuna''s business model is centered around a matching engine that pairs clients with the most suitable mental health expert based on their specific needs. Clients can book either a single session or a pack of sessions, and they can easily schedule, reschedule, and communicate securely with their assigned expert. The pricing varies depending on the expert, type of therapy, and duration of the therapy, providing flexibility and transparency to the clients. 

In addition to individual therapy, Nuna also offers specialized therapy for couples and children aged 3-18. The platform ensures privacy and security for both clients and experts, facilitating secure chat, video calls, and note-taking features. 

Nuna generates revenue through the fees paid by clients for the therapy sessions. The company''s value proposition lies in its accessibility, affordability, and personalized approach to mental health services, making therapy more accessible to a wider audience. 

