The company''s business model is centered on supplying 100% renewable electricity and gas to domestic and business customers. Its revenue is primarily generated from the sale of energy, with tariffs designed to optimize energy usage, such as the ''Agile'' tariff which offers dynamic pricing based on wholesale costs. Beyond retail energy, Octopus has diversified its revenue through technology licensing, smart home technology sales, and electric vehicle leasing and charging solutions. As of December 2025, Octopus is the largest supplier of domestic electricity and gas in the UK, serving 7.7 million households.

A core component of Octopus Energy''s strategy is its proprietary technology platform, Kraken. Developed in-house, Kraken is an end-to-end smart operating system that automates large parts of the energy supply chain, from billing and customer relationship management to managing grid flexibility. The platform uses AI and machine learning to optimize energy supply and demand, enabling smart tariffs and efficient grid management. Kraken has been licensed to other major energy suppliers, including E.ON, EDF Energy, and Origin Energy, and as of 2025, it was contracted to manage over 70 million customer accounts worldwide. In late 2025, Octopus announced it would spin off Kraken as a separate entity, valued at $8.65 billion.

Octopus Energy Group comprises several business divisions, including Octopus Energy Retail, Kraken Technologies, Octopus Energy Generation, Kraken Flex (which manages smart grid assets), and Octopus Electric Vehicles. The company has expanded internationally through a series of acquisitions of retail energy companies in Germany, Spain, France, Italy, and the US. Key funding rounds have significantly increased the company''s valuation, reaching approximately $9 billion by January 2024, with investments from entities like Generation Investment Management (co-founded by Al Gore), Canada Pension Plan Investment Board (CPPIB), and Tokyo Gas.

Keywords: renewable energy supplier, energy technology, Kraken platform, smart grid, dynamic tariffs, electricity retail, gas supply, EV leasing, heat pumps, green energy, demand response, energy management software, utility technology, decarbonization, customer service platform, energy generation, grid flexibility, asset management', '["corporate","data management","sales","corporate learning management systems","paas","Private Equity","chat","hris management","Venture Capital","web fonts","recruitment marketing","online form builders","advocacy marketing","marketing","Subscription","marketing automation","javascript graphics","customer relationship management","human resources","page builders","Energy Management System","frameworks and libraries","communication and collaboration","testing and qa","content management system","other advertising software","Affordable And Clean Energy (#7)","online video platforms","marketing analytics","marketing performance measurement","software development","it infrastructure","web frameworks","source code management","Smart Grid","open source","b2b","Energy","tag management","advanced analytics and data science","demand side platforms","team collaboration","widgets","web servers","enterprise mobility management","online review management","customer service","retail operations software","Hard Tech","Energy Providers","programming languages","documentation tools","Verified Unicorns and $1B Exits","Commission","audio-video-graphics","advertising","software","human resource","Manufacturing","Clean Energy","website builders","B2b Online Marketplace","web and application servers","miscellaneous","programming","cloud infrastructure computing","business intelligence","Grid Technology","javascript libraries","Verified Thoroughbreds","intelligence and analytics","video players","containers","advertising networks","Late stage","real user monitoring","analytics","devops","security","Sustainable Development Goals","issue trackers","Climate Te