The company was established to tackle the lack of transparency and time-consuming manual processes that smaller brands face when sourcing ingredients. By consolidating suppliers, invoices, and payments, Opply''s platform helps businesses reduce administrative tasks and costs. In June 2022, Opply secured $4 million in a seed funding round led by Chalfen Ventures and Anthemis Group, with participation from Entrepreneurs First. This capital was aimed at expanding its engineering and commercial teams to support its go-to-market strategy. 

Opply operates as a B2B marketplace connecting food and beverage brands with a network of verified suppliers. The platform uses AI to match brands with suitable suppliers and automates the procurement workflow, from sourcing to payment and delivery tracking. A key feature is its ability to pool orders from multiple SMEs, which allows smaller businesses to benefit from collective buying power and access better pricing without being subject to minimum order restrictions. The platform is free to use, with Opply charging a small fee on order management to cover administrative and coordination costs. The company''s business model is designed to save brands time and money, reporting an average cost saving of 20% and a reduction of two months in sourcing time. 

The platform serves a range of clients from start-ups to scale-ups and co-manufacturers. Core features include automated sourcing with personalized quotes, a centralized system for communication and documentation, real-time order tracking, and flexible payment terms. By providing access to transactable supplier data and managing procurement from order management to financing, Opply offers an end-to-end solution for supply chain management. 

Keywords: AI supply chain, F&B ingredient sourcing, B2B marketplace, food and beverage procurement, automated ingredient ordering, supply chain automation, supplier discovery, collective buying, food manufacturing, ingredient procurement platform, SME supply chain, beverage industry suppliers, food logistics, digital procurement, order management system, supply chain finance, verified suppliers, raw material sourcing, Chalfen Ventures, Anthemis Group', '["data management","database","software as a service","sales","recurring billing","photo galleries","Venture Capital","e-commerce platforms","web fonts","recruitment marketing","online form builders","Food Logistics & Delivery","marketing","cross-border e-commerce","SaaS","marketing automation","customer relationship management","page builders","Angel","frameworks and libraries","content management system","marketing analytics","marketing performance measurement","it infrastructure","web frameworks","database management","shopping cart","b2b","web platform extensions","widgets","web servers","software framework","programming languages","Commission","advertising","website builders","generative ai","web and application servers","miscellaneous","programming","business intelligence","e-commerce","javascript libraries","wordpress plugins","database management software","intelligence and analytics","analytics","platform as a service","javascript frameworks","Marketplace & ecommerce","Early stage","font scripts","applicant tracking systems","ui frameworks","accounting and finance","configuration management","Food","machine learning","Woman Founder","maps","web tools and plugins"]', '["startup","rising_star","vc_backed","funded"]', 85.88, 6800, 1, 4, 34090895, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:53:18.240Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:53:18.240Z');

