Passionfruit''s business model is based on a service marketplace. It offers a platform where businesses can hire marketing specialists for specific projects or ongoing work. These specialists have been pre-screened for their experience, skills, and professionalism, ensuring high-quality service delivery. The company also conducts regular check-ins to ensure the specialists maintain high standards throughout each project. 

The startup has demonstrated its effectiveness through several success stories. For instance, within two months of hiring a specialist through Passionfruit, the Nansen ‘Gas Tracker’ dashboard jumped from page 3 to page 1, reaching over 18,000 new searches per month. Another case saw a social media specialist increase engagement by over 500% for Miro, executing their top-performing organic campaign of all time.

Passionfruit generates revenue by charging a fee for the services provided by the specialists on its platform. This fee is likely a percentage of the payment made by the hiring business to the specialist. The company''s value proposition includes reducing onboarding time and training costs for businesses, as the specialists come with their expertise.

