Ramp Network operates in the cryptocurrency market, specifically in the area of cryptocurrency exchanges. It offers a platform that allows users to buy and sell over 70 of the most popular cryptocurrencies on major blockchain networks. The platform supports major global payment methods and is constantly adding new options.

The company''s business model is based on providing a seamless, end-to-end service for buying and selling cryptocurrencies. It offers an on-ramp service, which allows users to buy cryptocurrencies with fiat currency, and an off-ramp service, which enables users to sell their digital assets and convert them back into traditional currency. The platform is non-custodial, meaning users retain full control and ownership of their digital assets throughout the transaction process.

Ramp Network makes money by charging a fee for each transaction conducted on its platform. The fee structure is not explicitly stated but is likely based on a percentage of the transaction value.

In summary, Ramp Network is a global cryptocurrency exchange platform that provides a seamless and user-friendly way for businesses and individuals to buy and sell digital assets.

