The company operates on a freemium business model, offering basic features for free, while premium features are available through a subscription to Raycast Pro. This Pro version provides additional capabilities such as AI assistance, custom themes, and synchronization across multiple Macs. 

Raycast also offers an API for developers to build and publish their own extensions, creating a community-driven ecosystem of tools and applications. This not only enhances the functionality of the platform but also provides a potential revenue stream through the Raycast Store, where these extensions can be sold. 

In addition to its software offerings, Raycast has diversified its revenue streams by selling branded apparel. This not only generates additional income but also helps to build brand recognition and loyalty. 

In summary, Raycast is a technology startup that provides a productivity-enhancing platform for Mac users, with a business model based on both software subscriptions and merchandise sales. 

