The company is headed by directors Napier Bonnet and Claire Kelly. Napier, a music supervisor and composer since 2008, leverages his background in composition and production to develop bespoke music briefs and manage Ricall''s roster of composers and performers. The team has extensive experience negotiating multi-platform global campaigns and liaises with major rights holders worldwide. This ensures clients receive a thorough overview of available talent for their specific needs. 

Ricall also provides a platform for independent and unsigned artists to gain exposure through sync licensing opportunities. The company puts forward music from these artists for use in film, TV, and advertising. This service operates on a non-exclusive basis, allowing artists to retain the rights and control over their music. Ricall earns a 15% commission only when an artist''s track is licensed, creating a mutually beneficial relationship where the company is motivated to promote the artists'' work to filmmakers, videographers, and music supervisors. 

Keywords: music supervision, sync licensing, rights clearance, music for advertising, film music, TV soundtracks, bespoke music composition, music research, independent artist promotion, brand music, commercial music, music production services, re-record services, music for film trailers, social media music, sound branding, artist and label services, music clearance, corporate video music, music catalogue', '["Venture Capital","Angel","other advertising software","Video","uk is8 creative industries","widgets","Breakout stage","audio-video-graphics","advertising","Sharing Economy","miscellaneous","javascript libraries","Crowdsourcing","intelligence and analytics","video players","analytics","web analytics","b2c","javascript frameworks","font scripts","social networks","Music","rich text editors"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 20.67, 80, 0, 0, 7800000, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:54:12.521Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:54:12.521Z');

The core of Rungie''s business is to provide tools for brands, franchises, and content creators to connect with their audiences through community building, monetization, and loyalty programs. The platform leverages blockchain technology to enhance the relationship between creators and their followers. Clients are equipped with a suite of services for monetization, community management, and fostering loyalty. The business model appears to be centered on offering these platform-based services to a B2B market within the media and information services industry.

Rungie''s product portfolio includes several distinct projects. Overgie is a smart monetization platform designed to help creators generate new revenue streams while identifying and rewarding their most engaged community members through a points and ranking system. Berrly is a Software-as-a-Service (SaaS) solution aimed at simplifying the management of cultural associations, sports clubs, and non-profit organizations by automating workflows and centralizing member communications. Additionally, MITO Gallery serves as a space for digital art, allowing galleries and artists to connect with collectors and explore new avenues in the art world. Across its offerings, Rungie emphasizes security, with its platform being audited, and sustainability by utilizing energy-efficient technology.

Keywords: blockchain platform, community management, content creator monetization, fan engagement, loyalty programs, digital art, SaaS, B2B media services, venture capital, David Gabriel Tomuletiu, Overgie, Berrly, MITO Gallery, brand-audience connection, community building tools, smart monetization, artist services, franchise solutions, community gamification', '["Media","Venture Capital","Decentralised Applications","Subscription","SaaS","Blockchain","it infrastructure","web frameworks","b2b","web servers","software framework","Hard Tech","web & portal technology","web and application servers","javascript libraries","NFT","security","Early stage","ui frameworks"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 46.7, 430, 0, 0, 6818179, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"year":2022,"revenue":378788,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":6818179,"employees":22},{"year":2023,"revenue":1818181,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":6818179,"employees":21},{"year":2024,"revenue":1818181,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":6818179,"employees":17},{"year":2025,"revenue":1818181,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":6818179,"employees":17},{"year":2026,"revenue":1818181,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":6818179,"employees":11}]', '2026-11-05T15:56:04.243Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:56:04.243Z');

The platform''s business model is centered on streamlining the supply chain for healthcare providers. By aggregating products from numerous suppliers, Salupro offers a one-stop-shop for dental and veterinary supplies. The company also provides additional services such as dropshipping, which allows for direct shipment of products from the supplier to the end customer, further optimizing logistics and reducing inventory costs for clinics and stores.

Salupro''s target clients are primarily dental clinics, prosthetic laboratories, and veterinary clinics and stores. The platform is designed to meet the specific needs of these professional users, offering a tailored selection of products and a user-friendly interface for comparing and purchasing them. The company operates in the B2B e-commerce market for healthcare supplies, a sector that is increasingly moving towards digitalization and centralized procurement solutions.

