The company emerged from stealth in February 2026 with a $4.5 million seed funding round co-led by Northzone and Initialized Capital, with participation from Entrepreneur First, Nebular, and angel investors. Seamflow is addressing significant delays in the TIC sector, where complex documentation, audits, and reviews create long waiting periods for product approvals, particularly in the medical device industry in the EU. The company''s AI-first platform is designed to streamline and automate these workflows, targeting a global TIC market estimated at over $250 billion. 

Seamflow operates on a B2B subscription-based model, providing its end-to-end platform to certification bodies and enterprises in sectors like medical devices, automotive, and food safety across Europe, North America, and Asia. The software assists with the entire certification process, from intake and technical file review to decision-making and audit trails. Key features include document intelligence to extract evidence from reports, regulation-aware context for assessments, automated completeness checks, and AI-assisted report drafting. By reducing administrative tasks such as auditor scheduling and review coordination, the platform allows expert assessors to focus on substantive judgments, aiming to significantly shorten certification timelines. The company''s initial focus is on medical devices, but it is expanding to serve the broader industrial infrastructure market. 

Keywords: Testing Inspection and Certification, TIC, AI workflows, regulatory compliance software, product certification, compliance automation, medical device certification, document intelligence, audit management, B2B SaaS, regulatory technology, RegTech, quality management system, industrial infrastructure, certification bodies, notified body, automated compliance, technical review automation, AI-assisted reporting, market access, quality assurance technology', '["Venture Capital","Core AI","SaaS","page builders","Angel","frameworks and libraries","development","Facility Inspection and Maintenance Robots","performance","it infrastructure","web frameworks","customer data platforms","b2b","Artificial Intelligence","advanced analytics and data science","widgets","web servers","software framework","content delivery network","programming languages","miscellaneous","programming","Supply Chain Management","javascript libraries","intelligence and analytics","Enterprise Software","real user monitoring","analytics","operating systems & computing languages","web analytics","uk is8 digital and technologies","application development & management","javascript frameworks","Early stage","font scripts","ui frameworks","Industrial Robotics","machine learning","operating systems","web tools and plugins"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 79.83, 400, 1, 3, 20454537, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:55:23.556Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:55:23.556Z');

Secret Escapes operates in the luxury travel market, targeting consumers who seek premium travel experiences but are also price-conscious. The company negotiates exclusive rates with luxury hotels and holiday providers, ensuring that the offerings are hand-picked and meet high standards. This approach allows Secret Escapes to provide added perks and unique experiences to its members.

The business model is straightforward: Secret Escapes earns a commission from the travel providers for each booking made through its platform. This commission-based model aligns the company’s interests with those of its members, as it incentivizes Secret Escapes to secure the best possible deals. Additionally, the company may generate revenue through advertising and partnerships with travel-related businesses.

In summary, Secret Escapes leverages its large membership base and strong negotiating power to offer luxury travel at discounted rates. The company’s focus on quality and exclusivity sets it apart in the competitive travel market.

