The company was established in 2016 by Anthony Rose and Laurent Laffy. Rose, a software engineer by trade, previously led the BBC iPlayer team and later founded the social TV startup Beamly, which was acquired by Coty. Laffy brought his venture capital experience to the partnership, having been a managing partner at Accel Partners and an investor in several tech companies. This blend of technical and investment expertise shaped the company''s mission to streamline legal complexities for early-stage businesses.

SeedLegals provides a suite of tools that enable founders to create, negotiate, and sign all the necessary legal agreements for a funding round digitally. Its platform replaces the traditionally slow and expensive process of engaging law firms for these tasks. Key offerings include generating term sheets, shareholders'' agreements, and resolutions, as well as managing company share distributions and employee stock option plans through an automated cap table. The platform''s goal is to make these essential legal services more accessible, faster, and more affordable for the startup ecosystem.

The business model is based on a pay-as-you-go structure for specific legal products, such as closing a funding round or setting up an option scheme, as well as subscription plans for ongoing services like cap table management and legal support. This model caters to the varying needs and financial constraints of startups, from pre-seed to Series A and beyond. By serving founders, investors, and startup accelerators, SeedLegals has positioned itself as a key infrastructure provider within the UK and French startup scenes.

