The company''s core offerings are its HELOC and a more traditional Homeowner Loan. The Selina HELOC functions like a revolving credit facility secured against a property, allowing customers to draw, repay, and redraw funds as needed over a flexible period of up to five years. Interest is charged only on the funds drawn, and there are typically no early repayment charges. This product is positioned as an alternative to remortgaging or personal loans, offering the flexibility of a credit card with the lower interest rates of a mortgage. The Homeowner Loan is a standard second-charge mortgage for those who need a lump sum upfront. Both products cater to a variety of needs, including home improvements, debt consolidation, school fees, and business purposes. 

Selina Finance operates a digital-first model, featuring an online, paperless application process designed to be efficient for both direct customers and brokers. The company utilizes automated valuation models (AVMs) to speed up property valuations. Its clients are U.K. homeowners, and it distributes its products both directly and through a network of over 200 commercial finance and mortgage brokers. The business generates revenue from interest on the loans and through product and arrangement fees. 

Since its launch, Selina Finance has achieved several milestones. After gaining regulatory approval for consumer lending in 2020, it secured a £42 million Series A funding round. This was followed by a significant $150 million Series B round in February 2022, comprising $35 million in equity led by Lightrock and $115 million in debt from partners including Goldman Sachs. The company is a certified B Corporation, highlighting its commitment to social and environmental governance. 

Keywords: home equity line of credit, HELOC, secured loans, second charge mortgage, homeowner loan, property-backed lending, fintech, consumer lending, debt consolidation, home improvement finance, property finance, UK lender, digital lending, flexible credit, real estate equity, asset-backed lending, mortgage technology, financial services, property investment finance, alternative finance', '["personalization","data management","database","uk is8 financial services","paas","photo galleries","accounting","human resource management system","hris management","Venture Capital","web fonts","recruitment marketing","editors","ad exchanges","marketing","marketing automation","javascript graphics","customer relationship management","human resources","page builders","frameworks and libraries","communication and collaboration","development","identity and access management","content management system","Consumer Lending","Fintech","storage","other advertising software","risk and compliance","payroll management and benefits administration","it infrastructure","web frameworks","source code management","travel and expense management","database management","b2b","web platform extensions","tag management","it infrastructure & operations management","widgets","web servers","search engines","customer service","content delivery network","programming languages","Commission","Breakout stage","audio-video-graphics","advertising","website builders","web and application servers","miscellaneous","programming","caching","cloud infrastructure computing","office suites","javascript libraries","wordpress plugins","intelligence and analytics","video players","analytics","devops","security","operating systems & computing languages","cloud hosting","web analytics","platform as a service","a-b testing","b2c","javascript frameworks","fraud detection and prevention","live chat","communications technology","font scripts","Mortgages & Lending","cache tools","payroll processing","social networks","blogs"