Sourceful''s business model is centered around its innovative platform that allows clients to design, produce, and manage sustainable packaging solutions all in one place. The platform offers a range of tools, including a generative packaging design feature that uses AI to create unique packaging ideas in minutes. Clients can visualize and proof their packaging online using Sourceful Studio, which turns static 2D designs into animated 3D prototypes. This feature helps brands save time and reduce operational costs by allowing them to test new ideas quickly without waiting for physical samples.

The company generates revenue by offering its platform as a service to brands that need sustainable packaging solutions. Clients pay for the design, production, and management services provided by Sourceful. Additionally, Sourceful may earn income from partnerships with suppliers and other stakeholders in the packaging supply chain.

Sourceful''s mission is to use science and data to create the packaging the world needs, making the switch to sustainable packaging easier and more efficient. By providing a one-stop solution for sustainable packaging, Sourceful helps brands reduce their environmental impact while also streamlining their packaging processes.

