The company operates in the free-to-play mobile gaming market, generating revenue primarily through in-app purchases and partnerships. Its business model focuses on creating what it calls "forever games"—titles that are easy to start but offer long-term engagement through regular content updates and a strong community focus. This strategy has led to a portfolio of games with over 80 million downloads. The studio''s first major success was "Super Penguins," which accumulated over 20 million downloads and gained significant popularity in South Korea. This initial hit was followed by simulation games like "Adventure Town," "Food Street," and "Home Street," a life simulation game that attracted a $4 million Series A funding round led by Index Ventures in 2017. This investment was aimed at expanding the team and further developing "Home Street," including collaborations with major entertainment brands. 

Supersolid has since diversified its portfolio, venturing into competitive multiplayer with "Snake Rivals" and entering the Roblox platform with "RoPets." The development of "Snake Rivals," its first real-time multiplayer game, prompted a significant technological shift, with the company adopting Google Cloud''s infrastructure, including Agones and Kubernetes Engine, to manage game servers and ensure a smooth experience for a global audience. More recently, the studio released "Cook & Merge," which combines puzzle mechanics with a narrative-driven renovation meta-game. The company''s strategy involves creating high production value games designed for a broad, inclusive audience, supported by a diverse team of over 50 people. 

Keywords: mobile gaming, free-to-play, game development, in-app purchases, simulation games, life simulation, multiplayer games, game studio, Super Penguins, Home Street, Food Street, Snake Rivals, RoPets, Cook & Merge, Index Ventures, Ed Chin, Kenneth Fejer, Michelle Chuang, Tommy Chuang, Roblox developer, community-focused games', '["data management","database","corporate learning management systems","Venture Capital","web fonts","editors","ad exchanges","javascript graphics","customer relationship management","frameworks and libraries","communication and collaboration","testing and qa","content management system","online video platforms","performance","system analytics & monitoring","software development","web frameworks","wikis","uk is8 creative industries","team collaboration","widgets","content delivery network","programming languages","documentation tools","audio-video-graphics","advertising","human resource","web & portal technology","miscellaneous","programming","caching","business intelligence","javascript libraries","intelligence and analytics","video players","analytics","other audio-video-graphics software","devops","Gaming","issue trackers","cad & graphics","operating systems & computing languages","web analytics","visualisation software","Mobile Gaming","b2c","application development & management","javascript frameworks","live chat","Early stage","font scripts","cache tools","social networks","blogs","design","tools","ui frameworks","continuous integration","project management","Woman Founder","operating systems","web tools and plugins"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 65.08, 12000, 1, 1, 18181811, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:53:18.240Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:53:18.240Z');

Swap''s business model is centered around transforming returns from a cost burden into a growth engine. The platform provides a seamless exchange experience, allowing customers to receive the correct item before returning the incorrect one. This not only enhances customer satisfaction but also helps retailers save sales that might otherwise be lost.

In addition to managing returns and exchanges, Swap offers innovative working capital solutions. These include queued refunds and returns-based funding, which provide retailers with the financial flexibility to navigate seasonal cycles and other cash flow challenges. Essentially, Swap reimburses retailers for returns at times of their choosing, ensuring they have the necessary funds to continue operations smoothly.

Swap makes money through a combination of service fees and financing charges. Retailers pay for the platform''s returns and exchanges management services, as well as for the financial products that help them manage cash flow. By offering these integrated solutions, Swap not only improves the returns process but also supports the overall financial health of its clients.

In summary, Swap-Commerce.com is revolutionizing the e-commerce returns landscape by combining efficient returns management with flexible financing options, thereby helping online retailers enhance customer satisfaction and maintain healthy cash flow.

Keywords: returns management, exchanges, e-commerce, financing solutions, cash flow, queued refunds, returns-based funding, customer satisfaction, working capital, online retailers.', '["corporate","Venture Capital","Core AI","Subscription","SaaS","Angel","AI Agents","Circular Economy","uk is8 creative industries","b2b","Artificial Intelligence","AI Applications","Late stage","Marketing","uk is8 digital and technologies","Reverse Logistics"]', '["startup","colt","rising_star","vc_backed","funded"]', 92.64, 41000, 1, 24, 454545273, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '[{"year":2025,"revenue":20833325,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":181818109,"employees":230},{"year":2026,"revenue":20833325,"ebitda":null,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":454545273,"employees":382}]', '2026-11-05T15:53:04.860Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:53:04.860Z');

The company operates on a disruptive business model that eliminates traditional retail overheads like showrooms and warehouses, connecting consumers directly with manufacturers and artisans worldwide. This vertically integrated approach significantly shortens the supply chain, allowing Swoon to offer handcrafted, designer pieces at fair prices. A core feature of its strategy is a data-centric, ''test and scale'' approach to design and production. The in-house design team, The Swoon Studio, leverages data analytics and social trends to create new designs monthly—a much faster cycle than the industry standard. These designs are initially released in small batches to a community of ''Insiders'' to gauge demand in real-time. Only the most popular items are scaled up for full production, minimizing waste and ensuring product-market fit. This agile process allows the company to launch multiple new designs daily. 

Swoon targets style-conscious, savvy professionals who are passionate about their home environments. The product catalog is extensive, including sofas, tables, chairs, beds, and lighting. The company has also expanded its reach through strategic collaborations with major retailers like John Lewis & Partners and M&S, as well as kitchen manufacturer Harvey Jones. Since its inception, Swoon has secured significant venture capital funding from investors including Octopus Ventures and Index Ventures, raising a total of $44.2M over four rounds. 

