Symbe.co primarily serves sales teams and businesses that require robust and compelling business cases to drive their sales efforts. The platform is especially beneficial for companies looking to save time, money, and resources while ensuring high-quality outcomes. By providing ready-to-use templates, Symbe.co helps sales teams quantify and drive the highest value outcomes throughout the entire customer relationship cycle.

The business model of Symbe.co revolves around a subscription-based service, where clients pay for access to the platform and its features. This model ensures a steady revenue stream while providing clients with continuous updates and improvements to the platform. Additionally, Symbe.co offers an Early Access program and a CoDesign program, allowing users to shape the product based on their specific needs and insights. This collaborative approach not only enhances user satisfaction but also ensures that the platform evolves in line with market demands.

Symbe.co makes money by charging subscription fees for access to its platform. The company also benefits from the Early Access program, where clients can test the tool and provide feedback, ensuring that the final product meets their needs. By automating the creation of business cases and proposals, Symbe.co helps businesses streamline their sales processes, leading to increased efficiency and better sales outcomes.

In summary, Symbe.co is a forward-thinking company that leverages automation to improve sales processes. It serves sales teams and businesses in need of high-quality business cases, operates on a subscription-based model, and focuses on user collaboration to continuously enhance its platform.

Keywords: automation, business cases, sales efficiency, customer relationship, templates, subscription model, Early Access, CoDesign program, sales teams, business solutions.', '["Venture Capital","Core AI","Subscription","SaaS","Angel","b2b","Artificial Intelligence","programming","AI Applications","javascript libraries","Enterprise Software","uk is8 digital and technologies","Early stage","Machine Learning","web tools and plugins"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 81.28, 380, 0, 0, 25909081, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:56:04.243Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:56:04.243Z');

TOQIO''s core offering is a low-code/no-code platform that enables businesses, financial institutions, and non-financial corporations to create and launch their own fully branded banking and finance solutions. The platform is designed to significantly reduce the time-to-market for new financial products, allowing clients to deploy solutions in weeks rather than months or years. This is achieved by providing a configurable framework with over 300 UI elements, customizable workflows, and a marketplace of pre-integrated, third-party financial service providers. Clients can build and deploy solutions for various B2B use cases, such as creating new revenue streams, improving cash cycles, and integrating financial services directly into their existing ecosystems. 

The company''s business model is centered on its SaaS platform, which empowers corporates to act as distributors of financial products to their own ecosystems of SMEs, suppliers, or customers. This model addresses a market gap by making it easier for corporations to offer tailored financial products like payments and lending, while also helping SMEs access financial services they might otherwise struggle to obtain. TOQIO generates revenue by providing businesses with the tools to build, launch, and manage these financial solutions. The platform is sector-agnostic, with applications in industries ranging from food and beverage to logistics and retail. 

Since its inception, TOQIO has achieved several key milestones, including securing over 50 clients across Europe and expanding into the Spanish and US markets. The company has raised a total of $28.6 million over three funding rounds, including a significant Series A round of approximately €20 million ($19.2M) and a grant from Spain''s Centre for the Development of Industrial Technology (CDTI). Key investors include AlbionVC, Seaya, Speedinvest, and SIX FinTech Ventures. 

Keywords: embedded finance, fintech SaaS, low-code platform, B2B financial solutions, financial services integration, banking-as-a-service, custom finance apps, corporate finance, SME financing, payments orchestration', '["accelerator","uk is8 financial services","photo galleries","Venture Capital","web fonts","SaaS","javascript graphics","Angel","Banking","content management system","Fintech","storage","web frameworks","b2b","widgets","content delivery network","programming languages","Commission","Breakout stage","miscellaneous","cloud infrastructure computing","Financial Management Solutions","javascript libraries","intelligence and analytics","analytics","API","cloud hosting","web analytics","platform as a service","B2B SaaS for Banks","font scripts","blogs","maps","web tools and plugins"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 60, 3700, 0, 0, 93499963, -2190344, 2022, -3285662, 2025, '[{"year":2021,"revenue":715993,"ebitda":-787572,"profit":-648096,"rnd":null,"valuation":42727256,"employees":46},{"year":2022,"revenue":1236621,"ebitda":-2190344,"profit":-2192275,"rnd":null,"valuation":93499963,"employees":74},{"year":2023,"revenue":1236621,"ebitda":-2190344,"profit":-2192275,"rnd":null,"valuation":93499963,"employees":80},{"year":2024,"revenue":1578024,"ebitda":-2190344,"profit":-4327582,"rnd":null,"valuation":93499963,"employees":71},{"year":2025,"revenue":1329209,"ebitda":-2190344,"profit":-3285662,"rnd":null,"valuation":93499963,"employees":36},{"year":2026,"revenue":1329209,"ebitda":-2190344,"profit":-3285662,"rnd":null,"valuation":93499963,"employees":27}]', '2026-11-05T15:54:35.037Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:54:35.037Z');

The business model of Tangent is quite innovative. It offers a free platform for its members, providing them with training, coaching, and tools to create compelling video pitches. These pitches are then viewed by employees from top tech companies who can refer the candidates into their organizations. This referral process significantly increases the chances of getting hired, as employee referrals are known to be at least nine times more effective than traditional job applications.

Tangent makes money by partnering with tech companies that are looking to diversify their sales teams and improve their recruitment processes. These companies benefit from a pool of well-prepared candidates who have been trained and vetted by Tangent. Additionally, Tangent may offer premium services or partnerships with educational institutions and other organizations looking to support their students or members in career transitions.

In summary, Tangent connects diverse talent with tech sales opportunities through a combination of training, coaching, and employee referrals. It operates in the tech recruitment market and serves individuals looking to break into tech sales, as well as tech companies seeking diverse and qualified candidates.

Keywords: tech sales, recruitment, career development, diverse backgrounds, employee referrals, video pitches, coaching, training, job placement, tech companies.', '["accelerator","data management","Venture Capital","Jobs Recruitment","Advertising","SaaS","marketing automation","Angel","travel and expense management","b2b","advanced analytics and data science","team collaboration","content delivery network","Breakout stage","cloud infrastructure computing","javascript libraries","intelligence and analytics","analytics","issue trackers","b2c","Mentoring","accounting and finance","Human Resources","machine learning","project management"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 72.62, 32000, 1, 15, 3333332, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:54:51.538Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:54:51.538Z');

