The company operates in the online education market, targeting a diverse clientele that includes mid-level managers, entrepreneurs, and professionals seeking to upskill. Its business model is centered on providing high-quality, practical business education at a fraction of the cost of traditional MBA programs, with its flagship program priced at under $1,000. This direct-to-consumer (B2C) approach is complemented by a business-to-business (B2B) model, where companies like Google, EY, and Bain & Company integrate The Power MBA''s courses into their employee training programs. Revenue is generated through the sale of these online master''s programs.

The core offering is a fully online MBA alternative structured around the concept of microlearning, with daily classes delivered in 15-minute video segments. This flexible, self-paced format allows students to complete the program in approximately 10-11 months. The curriculum is designed to provide a comprehensive 360-degree view of business, covering modules such as business model innovation, lean startup methodologies, marketing strategies, finance, and leadership. A key feature is its faculty, which includes not only academics but also founders and executives from globally recognized companies like Netflix, YouTube, Waze, and Tesla, who provide insights through real-world case studies. While the program is not an accredited MBA, it focuses on delivering up-to-date, practical knowledge that students can immediately apply in their careers.

Keywords: online education, business school, microlearning, MBA alternative, professional development, digital marketing, entrepreneurship education, business strategy, corporate training, edtech, online courses, leadership training, finance education, startup education, upskilling, flexible learning, case study method, global community, career advancement, business fundamentals', '["corporate","personalization","Online Courses","Corporate Learning","customer relationship management","Education","Community Learning","Higher Education","Education Providers","Breakout stage","appointment scheduling","customer experience management","analytics","Upskilling and Reskilling","a-b testing","b2c","javascript frameworks","Lifelong and Consumer Learning","Marketplace & ecommerce","ui frameworks"]', '["startup","funded"]', 61.13, 90, 1, 6, NULL, NULL, NULL, -1060209, 2023, '[{"year":2022,"revenue":7671902,"ebitda":null,"profit":107730,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":300},{"year":2023,"revenue":8532827,"ebitda":null,"profit":-1060209,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":300},{"year":2024,"revenue":8532827,"ebitda":null,"profit":-1060209,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":300},{"year":2025,"revenue":8532827,"ebitda":null,"profit":-1060209,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":300},{"year":2026,"revenue":8532827,"ebitda":null,"profit":-1060209,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":300}]', '2026-11-05T15:55:36.049Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:55:36.049Z');

The company serves a diverse clientele, including educational institutions, financial organizations, and general consumers who are interested in gamified learning and problem-solving tools. By targeting these markets, Cauldron aims to leverage the power of gaming as a transformative platform for change.

Cauldron''s business model revolves around the development and distribution of its unique game products. One of its notable projects, Nestlums, has been recognized at the prestigious Design Week awards. This game is designed to teach children about financial literacy, effectively building the future of pocket money management for young users. The company generates revenue through the sale of its games, partnerships with educational and financial institutions, and potentially through in-app purchases or subscription models.

In summary, Cauldron is a forward-thinking company that uses the engaging nature of games to address real-world issues in finance and education. By creating products that are both entertaining and educational, Cauldron is well-positioned to make a significant impact in its target markets.

