The company follows a business-to-business-to-consumer (B2B2C) model, primarily generating revenue through subscriptions from organizations. Its clients include a wide range of sectors such as higher education, corporate employers, and public health organizations like the UK''s National Health Service (NHS), as well as government bodies. These partnerships provide access to the platform for large populations across the UK, US, Canada, and New Zealand. Togetherall operates as a for-profit social impact business, focused on being financially self-reliant while creating a measurable positive effect on wellbeing. 

The platform is designed for individuals dealing with mild to moderate mental health conditions like stress, anxiety, and depression. Its core feature is an anonymous online community where members can share their experiences and support one another. This peer interaction is monitored around the clock by more than 50 licensed mental health practitioners, referred to as Wall Guides, who ensure the safety of the environment and provide support. In addition to the community forum, Togetherall offers members a variety of self-guided courses and resources to help them manage their mental health. The company has secured at least $18.6M in funding over several rounds, including a significant $10 million investment in November 2020 led by FPE Capital to accelerate its North American expansion. 

Matthew McEvoy was appointed CEO in May 2023, succeeding Henry Jones. McEvoy previously led the company''s successful growth in North America, a key focus for the firm. He brings over 18 years of experience in the mental health services sector, including building a student support program at Morneau Shepell (now Telus Health). The leadership team also includes Chief Clinical Officer Ben Locke, Ph.D., a licensed psychologist who oversees the clinical framework that underlies the platform''s safety and support systems. 

