The company''s core business is providing a highly secure platform for sending, receiving, and storing files, aimed at large corporate clients. It targets sectors where data sensitivity is paramount, including banking, insurance, energy, healthcare, and public administration, counting numerous IBEX-35 companies among its clientele. The business model is designed to help organizations eliminate the use of unauthorized third-party tools, a phenomenon known as Shadow IT, by offering a sanctioned and secure alternative for file exchange. 

Tranxfer''s platform is engineered with a multi-layered security framework. It provides end-to-end encryption for data in transit (SSL/TLS) and at rest (AES-256), data loss prevention (DLP) modules, and full traceability through audit logs that track all views, downloads, and transfer expirations. To enhance security, it incorporates features like two-factor authentication and automatic file deletion. The service integrates seamlessly into existing corporate workflows, offering plugins for Microsoft Outlook, Microsoft Teams, and Google''s digital workplace, allowing employees to transfer files securely without leaving their familiar work environment. The product suite includes modules for secure file exchange, customizable data intake forms, virtual data rooms, and a replacement for traditional FTP/SFTP protocols. 

Keywords: secure file transfer, cybersecurity, data loss prevention, corporate file transfer, enterprise security, B2B SaaS, data encryption, compliance, audit trail, shadow IT, secure collaboration, digital workplace security, secure data storage, financial services security, IBEX-35, virtual data room, FTP replacement, secure communication, information protection, data security solutions', '["database","photo galleries","Venture Capital","web fonts","Subscription","SaaS","javascript graphics","Security","frameworks and libraries","content management system","Data protection","it infrastructure","b2b","web platform extensions","web servers","search engines","content delivery network","programming languages","audio-video-graphics","web and application servers","miscellaneous","programming","Cybersecurity","cloud infrastructure computing","e-commerce","Delivery","javascript libraries","wordpress plugins","intelligence and analytics","video players","analytics","web analytics","b2c","javascript frameworks","Early stage","font scripts","blogs","captcha","web tools and plugins"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 69.02, 20000, 0, 0, 4999998, NULL, NULL, -150388, 2023, '[{"year":2022,"revenue":565888,"ebitda":null,"profit":-169636,"rnd":null,"valuation":4999998,"employees":15},{"year":2023,"revenue":687761,"ebitda":null,"profit":-150388,"rnd":null,"valuation":4999998,"employees":23},{"year":2024,"revenue":687761,"ebitda":null,"profit":-150388,"rnd":null,"valuation":4999998,"employees":28},{"year":2025,"revenue":687761,"ebitda":null,"profit":-150388,"rnd":null,"valuation":4999998,"employees":28},{"year":2026,"revenue":687761,"ebitda":null,"profit":-150388,"rnd":null,"valuation":4999998,"employees":29}]', '2026-11-05T15:56:04.243Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:56:04.243Z');

The company has developed an innovative driver-to-driver relay system for Full Truckload (FTL) services, leveraging Big Data and Artificial Intelligence. This system is designed to minimize cargo standstill, thereby reducing road transit times. For drivers, the relay model facilitates more frequent returns home, promoting a better work-life balance.

