The business model functions as a marketplace, connecting users directly with official lottery administrations, thereby enabling these administrations to increase their sales via the internet. TuLotero makes money by acting as an e-retailer for lottery operators, though it does not charge users commissions on ticket purchases or winnings. Users can buy tickets for various national and European lotteries, such as Lotería Nacional, EuroMillions, Powerball, and Mega Millions, at the same price as physical retailers. The platform serves individual lottery players, providing a secure and digital way to store tickets, check results in real-time, and receive winnings. Prizes under a certain threshold (e.g., $600) are credited directly to the user''s in-app balance, which can then be withdrawn or used for future purchases. For larger prizes, the company''s prize department coordinates with the winner to facilitate the claim directly with the lottery commission. 

The application provides several features designed for user convenience and engagement. It allows users to play individually or form groups with friends and family to share bets and winnings, complete with a chat function. A key benefit is the digital storage of tickets, which prevents loss or damage. The service is available 24/7, and users can manage their accounts, set spending limits, and subscribe to their favorite numbers for automatic weekly plays. Having established a significant presence in Spain and Mexico, the company has expanded its operations to the United States. The platform is built on secure systems, complying with strict data protection regulations and undergoing regular audits to ensure the safety of transactions and user data. 

Keywords: mobile lottery, online lottery, lottery ticket app, digital lottery, EuroMillions, Powerball, lottery syndicates, group play lottery, lottery ticket management, state lottery sales, lottery results app, digital betting, secure lottery, online gambling, Lotería Nacional, play lottery online, lottery administration platform, lottery marketplace, mobile betting, subscription lottery', '["data management","social media marketing software","data security","Betting & Gambling","Outside Tech","ad exchanges","frameworks and libraries","communication and collaboration","development","deployment","other advertising software","online video platforms","risk and compliance","it infrastructure","web frameworks","source code management","open source","learning management system","widgets","web servers","search engines","software framework","App","programming languages","Commission","Breakout stage","audio-video-graphics","advertising","content marketing","site search","web and application servers","programming","cloud infrastructure computing","governance-risk and compliance","dev tools","javascript libraries","Betting & Gambling","intelligence and analytics","video players","analytics","devops","Gaming","security","operating systems & computing languages","web analytics","b2c","javascript frameworks","fraud detection and prevention","Marketplace & ecommerce","social networks","Mobile app","ui frameworks","certificates","continuous integration","configuration management","containerization","operating systems"]', '["funded"]', 28.67, 470000, 1, 1, NULL, 4008218, 2021, -110800, 2023, '[{"year":2016,"revenue":83333,"ebitda":-166667,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":null},{"year":2017,"revenue":250000,"ebitda":-50000,"profit":null,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":null},{"year":2018,"revenue":500000,"ebitda":333333,"profit":92394,"rnd":null,"valuation":null,"employees":null},{"year":2019,"revenue":833333,"ebitda":630542,"profit":134395,"rnd":null,"v