The company''s initial product is a zero-cost price comparison platform that enables SMBs to compare rates from payment providers like Worldpay, Barclaycard, and Revolut. This service was created to bring transparency to what is often an opaque and complex market, allowing merchants to find better rates for card payment processing and switch providers in minutes rather than days. This platform also feeds into distribution channels through partnerships with established comparison sites like uSwitch and Money.co.uk. 

Building on this foundation, Tuza is developing its core technology into a broader banking automation platform known as TuzaOS. This platform is designed to help large financial institutions grow by using AI agents to orchestrate and execute complex, regulated processes. The system eliminates manual tasks and workflows that can hinder scalability, allowing banks to automate operations from customer onboarding to checkout experiences. Tuza''s model includes forward-deployed engineers who embed within the client''s bank to integrate the platform and deliver returns within a short timeframe. 

Tuza has secured significant investment to fuel its growth, including a £1.5 million pre-seed round in 2023 followed by a £4 million seed round in May 2024. The seed round was led by Connect Ventures, with participation from Northzone, Triple Point, and Entrepreneur First. 

Keywords: banking automation, agentic workflows, AI agents, payment processing, SMB payment solutions, price comparison, FinTech, TuzaOS, merchant services, card payment providers, Ed Hardy, Olivia Stannah, Connect Ventures, Northzone, banking-as-a-service, regulated processes, workflow orchestration, customer onboarding automation, financial services technology', '["uk is8 financial services","Core Banking","Venture Capital","recruitment marketing","online form builders","editors","SaaS","human resources","Angel","communication and collaboration","content management system","Fintech","source code management","open source","travel and expense management","b2b","team collaboration","online review management","Embedded Finance","Commission","advertising","payment processing","website builders","e-commerce","javascript libraries","analytics","devops","platform as a service","Payment Processing","Early stage","applicant tracking systems","design","affiliate advertising networks","ui frameworks","accounting and finance"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 51.57, 1700, 0, 0, 9000000, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:55:23.556Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:55:23.556Z');

