The platform serves as an all-in-one solution for automating product lifecycle management and compliance. It addresses the challenges of fragmented data stored in spreadsheets and legacy systems by creating a centralized source for information on finished goods, formulations, packaging, and raw materials. Key features include a formulation designer that creates products to meet specific regulatory and client requirements, automated ingredient review, label creation, and regulatory filings. The system also offers tools for supplier relationship management, batch and test management, and project management to automate workflows and enhance collaboration across the supply chain. 

Co-founder Edward Alun-Jones is a three-time founder with experience in building and scaling B2B SaaS businesses. Co-founder Chris Gudde has a background in data science and has led large teams in risk and compliance, including a role as Head of Risk and Compliance at Heathrow Airport. Their combined expertise addresses the complexities of regulatory compliance in the cosmetics industry. 

In September 2023, Worldover announced it had raised £3 million in a seed funding round led by Index Ventures and Chalfen Ventures, with participation from Entrepreneur First and Plug and Play Ventures. This funding was intended to support the global launch of its automation system. The company aims to reduce the time and costs associated with ensuring product compliance, which can represent up to 1% of a company''s total revenue. 

Keywords: cosmetic compliance platform, product lifecycle management, AI automation, beauty industry software, regulatory automation, formulation design, supply chain management, B2B SaaS, ingredient data management, compliance workflows, chemicals industry software, manufacturing operations, supplier relationship management, batch management, label creation, regulatory filings, cosmetics data platform, automated data extraction, project management for cosmetics, beauty tech', '["Venture Capital","recruitment marketing","Subscription","SaaS","frameworks and libraries","development","b2b","programming languages","web & portal technology","Legal","uk is8 professional business services","platform as a service","javascript frameworks","Early stage","font scripts","applicant tracking systems"]', '["startup","vc_backed","funded"]', 83.08, 15000, 1, 3, 18000000, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-11-05T15:53:18.240Z', 'GBP', '2026-11-05T15:53:18.240Z');

