The core product is a credit card that allows users to earn points on their spending. These points can be redeemed for a variety of experiences, including dining at restaurants, flights on any airline, and other curated activities. This suggests a focus on a lifestyle-oriented customer segment that values experiences over simple cashback or merchandise rewards.

The market Yonder operates in is the competitive credit card and financial services industry in the UK, with a specific focus on the London market. Its target clients are likely young professionals and individuals with a disposable income who are interested in travel and lifestyle benefits.

Yonder differentiates itself by offering flexibility in rewards redemption, such as using points for flights on any airline at any time, and by curating a selection of high-quality dining and entertainment experiences for its members. The absence of foreign exchange fees is another key feature that would appeal to its target demographic of frequent travelers.

