Spector, a professor of genetic epidemiology, had a personal health scare that motivated him to create ZOE. He partnered with Jonathan Wolf, who has a background in physics and technology, and George Hadjigeorgiou, an entrepreneur who founded and sold a large online food delivery company. Wolf''s experience is in machine learning, while Hadjigeorgiou''s came from a personal interest in nutrition after discovering he had high cholesterol. The trio launched ZOE after securing initial funding to conduct the world''s largest nutrition science study, known as the PREDICT studies, in collaboration with institutions like King''s College London, Harvard, and Stanford.

The company''s direct-to-consumer business model begins with customers purchasing an at-home test kit. This kit includes a stool sample test for gut microbiome analysis, a blood fat test, and a continuous glucose monitor (CGM) worn for two weeks to measure blood sugar responses. Based on the data from these tests, ZOE''s AI-powered app provides personalized food scores, recipes, and dietary recommendations. Revenue is generated from the initial sale of the test kit and a recurring monthly subscription for access to the app and its features. The company also offers a whole-food supplement called Daily30+. Originally launched in the UK, the program is now available in the US. Before launching its nutrition product, the company developed the ZOE COVID Symptom Study app during the pandemic, which became the largest community-led COVID-19 study in the world and helped identify key symptoms of the virus.

Keywords: personalized nutrition, gut microbiome, metabolic health, at-home testing, AI, data science, health-tech, nutritional science, continuous glucose monitoring, blood fat analysis, subscription model, direct-to-consumer, Tim Spector, Jonathan Wolf, George Hadjigeorgiou, PREDICT study, food as medicine, health and wellness, diet personalization, microbiome testing, metabolic response', '["Health Platform","corporate","data management","social media marketing software","database","medical testing","software as a service","online community software","Biotechnology","photo galleries","human resource management system","Venture Capital","web fonts","recruitment marketing","BioTechnology","visual and user generated content marketing","supply chain management","marketing","Subscription","SaaS","javascript graphics","human resources","Innovative Food","Good Health And Well-Being (#3)","Angel","frameworks and libraries","communication and collaboration","development","content management system","online video platforms","system analytics & monitoring","DT and LS","payroll management and benefits administration","it infrastructure","web frameworks","Metabolism","travel and expense management","advanced analytics and data science","widgets","web servers","Digital Care","enterprise mobility management","software framework","uk is8 life sciences","Hard Tech","content delivery network","programming languages","social media analytics and monitoring","audio-video-graphics","website builders","miscellaneous","programming","Spinout","business intelligence","Weight Management","warehouse management","javascript libraries","UKSU","Zero Hunger (#2)","intelligence and analytics","video players","Late stage","analytics","inventory and order management","devops","security","Sustainable Development Goals","science-based","Nutrition","operating systems & computing languages","data integration","electronic signatures","Health","b2c","javascript frameworks","Food as Medicine","Testing","